##f$notes##
//*****************************************************************************
//
//  ScarletBeast - POWER HOLD'EM   (OpenPPL, No-Limit Texas Hold'em)
//  ===========================================================================
//
//  A complete NLHE strategy distilled from TWO source texts:
//
//    [N]  Daniel Negreanu - "Small Ball"   (Power Hold'em Strategy, 2008)
//    [B]  Doyle Brunson   - "Power Poker"   (Super System, NLHE section)
//
//  The two philosophies are deliberately blended and made selectable through a
//  single STYLE dial (see 05_config / f$Style):
//
//    Style 0  SMALL BALL  [N] - small bets (2.5x opens, ~60% c-bets), wide but
//             positional, pot control, never stack off without the near-nuts,
//             "don't go broke with one pair", low river-bluff frequency.
//    Style 1  POWER POKER [B] - aggressive, ~pot-sized bets, c-bet ~90% as the
//             pre-flop raiser, semi-bluff strong draws all-in, lead big hands
//             into the raiser, "bet with an out".
//    Style 2  HYBRID (default) - small-ball sizing/discipline with Brunson's
//             draw aggression and high c-bet frequency.
//
//  Both authors agree on the engine of the strategy and that agreement is the
//  spine of this profile:
//    * Position is power - play more, and more aggressively, in position. [N,B]
//    * Speculative hands (suited connectors, small pairs, suited aces) win the
//      big pots; play them cheaply to flop a monster.                     [N,B]
//    * Be the aggressor; pick up the many small uncontested pots.         [N,B]
//    * Play the OPPONENT'S hand, not just your own - so this profile is
//      opponent-aware via the PokerTracker HUD stats (see 10_opponents).  [N,B]
//    * Mix it up / stay unpredictable - balanced frequencies via randomround. [N,B]
//
//  THIRD SOURCE - the mental/discipline layer:
//    [T]  Larry W. Phillips - "The TAO of Poker" (285 rules, 2003)
//  TAO is a discipline + low-limit text; its rules are incorporated as follows:
//    * TIGHT SELECTION / PATIENCE - "see how many hands you can fold; make each hand
//      prove it is good." Reflected in the by-position open lists (20_lists) + the
//      fold-heavy default of every street. Discipline must hold "until the end." [T R10,R11]
//    * BET YOUR PREMIUMS - "start with premium hands; when you get them, bet them."
//      Reflected in list3betValue/list4betValue + the raise branches.            [T R3]
//    * VALUE OVER BLUFF IN LOW-LIMIT - the freeroll field calls too much, so bluffing
//      donates. f$CbetFreq dialed down (05_config), c-bet air CHECKED vs a station
//      (50_flop f$Opp_IsStation), 3-bet bluffs gated on a foldy/loose opp only.   [T R188-190, Ch.6]
//    * FOLD WHEN BEAT / DON'T PAY OFF - "if you're beat, fold; forget the idea they're
//      bluffing." Reflected in pot-control + bluff-catch discipline, and the river
//      never-bluff-a-station / fold-to-strength lines.                            [T Ch.3,R28]
//    * RESPECT THE CONFIDENT BAD PLAYER - don't bluff-catch light vs a maniac. [T R189]
//    * STAY UNPREDICTABLE - mix frequencies (randomround) rather than play face-up. [T R191]
//  The mental-game rules (tilt, calm, losing, luck, slumps, trusting your read) live in
//  the Lilith poker-coach (mcp/poker_coach_hype.py) - that is where TAO mostly applies.
//
//  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  TIER-1 LIBRARY EXPANSION (2026-06-15) - the relevant NLHE subset of the
//  PokerBooks library, distilled and reconciled into the dials above. Each new
//  source carries a citation tag used inline in 05_config / 20_lists / 10_opponents:
//
//    [HoH] Harrington on Hold'em I-II (Harrington & Robertie); [HoH2] = Vol-II page
//          cites - the M-ratio / inflection-point endgame. Drives f$M / f$Mzone and
//          the antes-aware push/fold + short-stack triggers. "First-in vigorish" as M falls.
//    [KE]  Kill Everyone / [KP] Kill Phil (Nelson, Rodman, Streib, Heston) -
//          CSI stages, equilibrium (Nash) push/fold, ICM bubble factor. Drives
//          the bubble-tightened ICM call gate and the move-in-or-fold short game.
//    [SSNL] Small Stakes No-Limit Hold'em (Miller/Mehta/Flynn) - SPR & COMMITMENT.
//          Drives f$SPR / f$Committed: the low-SPR branch of "don't go broke with
//          one pair" (at low SPR you SHOULD stack off top pair / overpair).
//    [ToP] Theory of Poker / [SM] Hold'em for Advanced Players (Sklansky/Malmuth)
//          - Fundamental Theorem, semi-bluff math, the Gap Concept, optimal bluff
//          frequency. Confirms the listCallOpen < listOpen* gap and the semibluff lines.
//    [CtM] Crushing the Microstakes (Williams) - exploit weak/passive fields:
//          value BIG vs stations (f$BetPctVsStation), broadened station typing,
//          never bluff the fish on any street.
//          DEEPENED 2026-06-20 (the freeroll/low-stakes field is our home game, so
//          this is the highest-value book): added the missing SLP archetype
//          (f$Opp_IsSLP, ~24/6) + the bet-pattern reads f$Opp_MinBetLead /
//          f$Opp_NutsyRaise ("turn/river raises are the nuts", "min/probe bets are
//          weak"); EXTRACTION/fastplay value-big extended to station+fish+SLP on all
//          three streets; "give up when they fight back" wired as the f$OppRepresents
//          respect-fold (fold one pair/overpair to a credible nut line, fold to
//          turn/river raises); fish bluff missed draws -> capped river value-call;
//          vs a nit/passive 3-bet fold even QQ/JJ/AK, flat (not 3-bet) into a nit's
//          tight open. See 12_aggressor.ohf + 40/50/60/70 [CtM p.NN] cites.
//    [PMM] Poker Math That Matters (Gaines) / [MoH] Math of Hold'em (Moshman) -
//          exact pot odds (f$RequiredEquity), fold-equity / MDF, the 15x set-mine
//          rule (f$SetMineOK, tighter than the old 10% f$WithinSpecRisk).
//    [SNG] SNG Blueprint / Moshman SNG / [SoS] Shaw "Secrets of Sit'n'gos" - stage
//          & bubble play. Drives f$Stage / f$NearBubble / f$BubbleTighten + the
//          listCallShove/listCallShoveBubble split and f$HeadsUpTourney. ([SoS] is
//          cited inline as its own tag where Shaw's bubble/HU calls are specific.)
//    [V6]  "How to Beat 6-Max Cash" (Vosti) - 6-max range widths; drives f$Is6Max
//          and the listOpenEP6 / listOpenMP6 6-max open branch (with [RF]).
//    [EM]  Ed Miller "Playing the Player" / "How to Read Hands" / [TN] Tri Nguyen
//          "Poker Blueprint" - stat-based opponent typing: the new TAG/LAG/fish/
//          maniac archetypes in 10_opponents (fixes IsAggro firing on AF alone).
//          ALSO (2026-06-20) the READ-THE-LINE story engine f$OppRepresents
//          (12_aggressor): infer the opponent's perceived range from his BETTING
//          LINE (checked-to / capped / merged / strong) and gate value/bluff/fold
//          on it - Miller's "play the player, read the line not the cards."
//
//  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  TIER-2 WAVE-1 LIBRARY EXPANSION (2026-06-15) - cash/MTT/SNG/HU technique. 18
//  books, deployed live, lint/parse clean (full legend + per-book deltas in
//  BOOKS_PROGRESS.md). These tags are also bundled at the head of the Tier-2 dials
//  in 05_config; registered here so EVERY inline tag resolves from this file:
//
//    [PNL] Flynn/Mehta/Miller "Professional No-Limit Hold'em" - the hand-class-aware
//          SPR/commitment bands (f$Committed; corrected the Tier-1 flat SSNL version).
//    [HC]  Harrington on Cash Games - deeper-stack value/commitment & the donk/min-bet
//          read; the tighter ~25x set-mine floor vs a nit (f$SetMineOK).
//    [RE]  Bertok/Nelson "The Raiser's Edge" - re-steal/3-bet-jam band (f$ReshoveSpot,
//          listReshove) and the <=15bb all-in zone.
//    [JL]  Jonathan Little "Secrets of Pro Tournament Poker" - the same re-steal band.
//    [ASH] Danny Ashman "Secrets of Short-handed NL" - short-handed barreling.
//    [EG]  Seidman "Easy Game" / [ER] Nguyen "NL Workbook: Exploiting Regulars" (the
//          [W] workbook) / [LTBR] "Let There Be Range" (Nguyen/CTS) - the double-barrel
//          gate (f$DoubleBarrel) and opponent-typed 3-bet-bluff freq (f$ThreeBetBluffFreq).
//    [DFR] "Dynamic Full Ring Poker" (Splitsuit) - full-ring tightening / the c-bet cap.
//    [RF]  Ryan Fees 6-max NL guide - the 6-max EP/MP open widths (with [V6]).
//    [HUM] Moshman "Heads-Up No-Limit" / [HUSNG] Mersenneary HUSNG guide - the HU open/
//          defend widths (listOpenHU/listDefendHU) and HU open size (f$Open_RaiseTo_HU).
//    [SNF] Snyder "Tournament Formula" / [SYS] "Systematic SNG" / [NSS] Shaw "Secrets of
//          Non-Standard SNGs" - structure-speed & DON/satellite survival (specified, mostly
//          DEFERRED to backlog; cited where a live dial leans on them, e.g. the all-in zone).
//
//  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  TIER-2 WAVE-2 LIBRARY EXPANSION (2026-06-15) - MTT decision-logs, Gordon's
//  combinatoric NLHE, and the strategic-restraint / opponent-exploitation
//  philosophy layer. Most of the ~30 books mined this wave were FIXED-LIMIT or
//  pure-intro and fully subsumed (see BOOKS_PROGRESS.md); the net-new deltas are:
//
//    [WPT1/WPT2] Turner/Lynch/Fleet "Winning Poker Tournaments One Hand at a
//          Time" v1/v2 - hand-by-hand MTT logs. NET-NEW: (1) the SB opens BIGGER
//          (~3x) because it plays the whole hand OOP -> SB branch in f$OpenBase;
//          (2) set-mining "is out of the question at THIS stage" once stacks are
//          shallow / squeeze-risk is high -> f$SetMineOK now stage-gated (f$Stage).
//    [GG]  Phil Gordon "Little Gold Book" - modern HUD/combinatoric NLHE. NET-NEW:
//          (1) board HIGH-CARD texture for c-bet bluffs - K/A/Q-high dry flops miss
//          a flat-caller's range (bluff), J/T-high dry flops HIT it (don't); low
//          disconnected "parched" boards barrel relentlessly -> f$BoardHighCardFoldy
//          / f$BoardParched (30_classify) gating the air c-bet (50_flop);
//          (2) turn bet-sizing geometry TurnBet=(EffStack-PotSize)/3 to set up a
//          clean pot-sized river jam -> f$TurnBetGeo (05_config, available symbol).
//    [Tao] Tao Te Ching (Lao Tzu) - wu-wei / water / yielding: the strategic-
//          RESTRAINT layer. Reinforces (as citations) the dialed-DOWN bluff freqs
//          (over-bluffing is forcing), don't-go-broke pot-control, and adapt-to-
//          depth/opponent. Mental-game rules route to Lilith, not here.
//    [SunTzu] Sun Tzu "Art of War" - know-enemy-and-self, deception, attack-
//          weakness/avoid-strength, win-without-fighting, terrain=position, "leave
//          a golden bridge for a retreating army". The OPPONENT-EXPLOITATION layer;
//          almost all already implemented. NET-NEW: "do not press a desperate foe"
//          -> f$Opp_PotCommitted (10_opponents) gating bluffs vs a cornered low-M
//          villain who cannot fold. Cited across 05_config/10_opponents/50-70.
//    [48L]/[Prince] Greene "48 Laws of Power" / Machiavelli "The Prince" - a
//          power-realism gloss on TAG poker (control info, crush the weak, ration
//          aggression, stay unpredictable). Every machine-observable principle is
//          ALREADY a live dial; added as CITATION REINFORCEMENT only, no behavior
//          change. Interpersonal/statecraft laws are out of scope (Lilith coach).
//    [LGY] Largay "NL: A Complete Course" - intro NLHE; every concept already
//          encoded (implied/reverse-implied odds, value-sizing, player typing,
//          game selection). NO new dial. [CNL] Cloutier/McEvoy, [AOW] Apostolico
//          "Art of War" poker, [HCC] Gaines "Hole Card Confessions", [ANL]/[EoP]/
//          [IPP]/[8M]/[PPM]/[PMVT]/[MC]/[NW]/[PKR] - mined, deltas either already
//          present or unimplementable (range/combinatoric/multi-hand-memory); the
//          backlog items are logged in LIMITATIONS.md.
//
//  Concepts the OHF/Hiss engine cannot express (per-opponent bubble factor, true
//  Nash/ICM solver, node-by-node range narrowing, multi-street line planning,
//  size-bucketed fold stats, real lobby payout curve, opponent steal-frequency
//  HUD stats, 4-bet-bluff range, open-size-relative 3-bet sizing, "shortest stack
//  yet to act" reshove-aware opening) are tracked as engine work in LIMITATIONS.md.
//  Remaining on-target books are queued in BOOKS_PROGRESS.md.
//
//  Bet amounts are expressed as RaiseTo <big blinds> (pre-flop) or
//  RaiseBy <pct> % (post-flop pot-fractions). Hiss converts the resulting
//  f$betsize into the table's chip amount.
//
//  This file is SEGMENTED across several .ohf files for maintainability
//  (00_notes, 05_config, 10_opponents, 12_aggressor, 15_explain, 16_steering,
//   20_lists, 30_classify, 40_preflop, 50_flop, 60_turn, 70_river, 90_table).
//   12_aggressor = cross-street aggressor rhythm (f$IAmAggressor/f$AggressorIsOpp/
//   f$ActBeforeAggressor + the f$ConservativeKnob/f$AggressorKnob dials, which also
//   modulate f$CbetFreq) + the f$OppRepresents read-the-line story engine. They
//   share one f$ namespace. They are either concatenated into one master .ohf, or dropped
//   into Hiss's bot_logic\Strategy\ folder and auto-loaded (see release notes).
//
//  TUNE the STYLE dial and the thresholds in 05_config to taste.
//
//*****************************************************************************

//=============================================================================
//  prwin (Monte-Carlo equity) configuration
//=============================================================================

##f$prwin_number_of_iterations##
20000

##f$prwin_number_of_opponents##
// Simulate against the opponents still contesting the pot.
WHEN Others RETURN nopponentsplaying FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  05_config - the STYLE dial and all tunable thresholds.
//  Edit the single RETURN line in f$Style to switch playing styles.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$Style##
// 0 = Small Ball [N]   1 = Power Poker [B]   2 = Hybrid (default)
// Runtime steering: the Terminal command "/strategy smallball|power|hybrid" sets
// openai_steer_anchor (11/12/13) and retunes the whole profile live. [steering]
WHEN openai_steer_anchor == 11 RETURN 0 FORCE
WHEN openai_steer_anchor == 12 RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN openai_steer_anchor == 13 RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 2 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  RUNTIME SYNAPSE-HARMONIZER KNOBS [Emrald 2026-06-21]
//  Three live 0..1 dials pushed from the Synapse Harmonizer tab via /api/knob
//  (engine symbols openai_knob_openrange / openai_knob_aggro / openai_knob_bluff;
//  DEFAULT 0.5 = NEUTRAL = today's behavior). No rebuild to retune - turn the dial.
//    openrange  1 = open MANY more hands  ...  0 = open far fewer (tight)
//    aggro      1 = bet/raise much more often  ...  0 = passive (check/call)
//    bluff      1 = bluff much more often  ...  0 = bluff almost never (value-only)
//  openrange retunes the preflop open tree (40_preflop); aggro scales f$CbetFreq;
//  bluff scales every dedicated bluff frequency (3-bet bluff, barrels, stabs).
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$OpenRangeKnob##
// The OBSERVER branch's open-range target takes the wheel when a branch is live (obsbranch>=1, fresh-
// gated to 0 by the engine when the brain is quiet); else the human/synapse openrange knob.
WHEN obsbranch >= 1 RETURN obsbranch_openrange FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_openrange FORCE

##f$OpenWiden##
// Knob turned UP past neutral -> open the wide ~65% steal range from late / the SB.
WHEN f$OpenRangeKnob >= 0.62 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$OpenTightenHard##
// Knob turned DOWN past neutral -> open only the MP-strength range from every seat.
WHEN f$OpenRangeKnob <= 0.30 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$AggroFreqMult##
// Multiplies the c-bet / aggression FREQUENCY. 0.5 (neutral) -> 1.0x; 0 -> 0.55x
// (passive); 1 -> 1.45x (relentless). Clamped to <= 0.95 downstream in f$CbetFreq.
// INTROSPECTION (fires only on a CONFIDENT read; base knob logic unchanged otherwise): press
// relentlessly vs a villain who over-folds / gives up the lead / is steaming.
WHEN f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp OR f$Exploit_Tilt RETURN 1.35 FORCE
WHEN obsbranch >= 1 RETURN 0.55 + obsbranch_aggro * 0.9 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.55 + openai_knob_aggro * 0.9 FORCE

##f$BluffFreqMult##
// Multiplies every dedicated BLUFF frequency (3-bet bluff, double / triple barrel, stabs).
// 0.5 (neutral) -> 1.0x; 0 -> 0.55x (value-only); 1 -> 1.45x (high bluff).
// INTROSPECTION takes PRECEDENCE (fires only on a confident read): NEVER bluff a villain who won't
// fold (station / sticky bettor / steamer); CRANK bluffs vs one who over-folds; otherwise the base
// bluff knob is unchanged.
WHEN f$Exploit_NeverFolds OR f$Exploit_KeepsFiring OR f$Exploit_Tilt RETURN 0.2 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp OR f$Exploit_Folds3Bet RETURN 1.4 FORCE
WHEN obsbranch >= 1 RETURN 0.55 + obsbranch_bluff * 0.9 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.55 + openai_knob_bluff * 0.9 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Stack-depth regime (in big blinds).  Small ball requires depth; once short,
//  both authors revert to a tight raise/limp-or-push game. [N pp.33-34][B S8.3]
//  YIELD AND FLOW to the depth: the stiff/unyielding plan dies, the soft/adaptive
//  one lives. [Tao ch.76 "the stiff and unyielding is the disciple of death; the
//  soft and yielding, of life"][Tao ch.78 "water overcomes the hard"][SunTzu X
//  "terrain" -> depth & position dictate the line][Prince "adapt to the times"].
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$EffStack##
// Effective stack in big blinds (capped at the largest opponent we can lose to).
WHEN EffectiveMaxStacksizeOfActiveOpponents < StackSize RETURN EffectiveMaxStacksizeOfActiveOpponents FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN StackSize FORCE

##f$DeepStack##
// Above ~60bb: full small-ball / speculative play is profitable.
WHEN f$EffStack >= 60 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ShortStack##
// Below ~25bb: stop limping speculative hands, tighten, prefer raise-or-fold.
// Also true in the Orange M-zone or worse (M<=10) for ante tables. [HoH2 p131-138]
WHEN f$Mzone <= 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack <= 25 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$PushFoldStack##
// Push/fold (jam, don't min-raise) at <= 15bb. Raised 10 -> 13 -> 15: HUMAN FEEDBACK
// (learner_decisions #42: liked jamming QJs at 12.5bb instead of min-raising) [N p.34], then
// the SNG/HU canon's "all-in zone" is <=15bb [NSS p106][RE p2375].
// Antes-aware: also jam in the Red/Dead M-zone (M<=5), which with live antes can be
// reached at a higher bb-count than 15. Additive - never removes the 15bb behavior. [HoH2 p140]
// This 15bb ceiling is the system-wide push/fold boundary: it hands off cleanly to f$ReshoveSpot
// (the 15<EffStack<=25 re-steal band) at exactly 15bb, with no gap or overlap.
WHEN f$Mzone <= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack <= 15 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Position helpers (relative to the field still to act / the raiser).
//  Position is power - the terrain that decides the battle; play more, and more
//  aggressively, in position. [SunTzu X "the general who knows the ground will
//  conquer"][48L L35/L48 "control the field, stay formless"].
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$InPositionPre##
// We are last (or near-last) to act before the flop.
WHEN InButton OR InCutOff RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$InPositionPost##
// We are last (or near-last) to act after the flop.
WHEN InButton OR InCutOff RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HandIsHeadsup AND NOT InSmallBlind RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HeadsUpPot##
// Exactly one opponent left contesting this pot.
WHEN nopponentsplaying <= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Pre-flop sizing (RaiseTo, in big blinds).  Both authors raise BIGGER over
//  limpers (isolation) - we add 1bb per limper. [N p.24][B]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$OpenBase##
// Standard first-in open size.
// SB opens BIGGER (~3x): it plays the WHOLE hand out of position, so deny a cheap
// flop / size up to discourage the BB flat. Only when not in the push/fold band
// (there we jam, not min-raise) and not heads-up (the HU SB has its own size,
// f$Open_RaiseTo_HU). [WPT1 "I ALWAYS raise to 3x the BB from the SB"]
WHEN InSmallBlind AND NOT f$PushFoldStack AND NOT f$HeadsUpPot RETURN 3.0 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 3.5 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 2.5 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 2.5 FORCE

##f$Open_RaiseTo##
// Add one big blind for each limper we are isolating. Scaled by f$ICM_SizeMult (ICM chip value).
WHEN Others RETURN (f$OpenBase + Calls) * f$SizeMult FORCE

##f$Iso_RaiseTo##
// PUNISH limpers (1bb bettors): iso-raise over the limp, +1bb per extra limper. But DON'T always slam
// the big ~5bb punish -- mix the size with randomround so we're not face-up: ~12% a ~2bb min-raise
// (cheap iso / trap), ~25% 3bb, ~28% 4bb, ~35% the full 5bb. Stays balanced + harder to read.
// [Emrald: don't always 5-bet limpers -- vary 2/3/4/5bb]
WHEN randomround < 0.12 RETURN (1 + Calls) * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN randomround < 0.37 RETURN (2 + Calls) * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN randomround < 0.65 RETURN (3 + Calls) * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN (4 + Calls) * f$SizeMult FORCE

##f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo##
// 3-bet sizing (to N big blinds). Larger out of position. [N pp.26-27]
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 13 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN f$InPositionPre RETURN 9 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 11 * f$SizeMult FORCE

##f$FourBet_RaiseTo##
// 4-bet for value vs a 3-bet.
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 26 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 22 * f$SizeMult FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Post-flop bet sizing (as a percentage of the pot).  Same size for value and
//  for bluffs - never telegraph. [N p.37-38][B "reasonable bet"]
//  Wet (draw-heavy) boards get a larger bet to charge draws. [N p.231 analog]
//  Uniform value=bluff sizing + randomized frequencies = formlessness/deception:
//  the villain cannot read our hand from our size. [SunTzu I.18 "all warfare is based
//  on deception"][SunTzu VI "be so subtle you are formless"][48L L4 "always say less
//  than necessary"][Prince/IPP "consistent bet-sizing hides information"].
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$BetPctFlop##
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 85 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 AND (FlushPossible OR StraightPossible) RETURN 66 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 55 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN (FlushPossible OR StraightPossible) RETURN 75 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 60 * f$SizeMult FORCE

##f$BetPctTurn##
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 90 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 60 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 70 * f$SizeMult FORCE

##f$BetPctRiver##
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 90 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 55 * f$SizeMult FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 66 * f$SizeMult FORCE

##f$TurnBetGeo##
// Turn bet-sizing GEOMETRY (in big blinds, NOT a pot-%): size the turn bet so the
// river is auto-set to a clean pot-sized shove. TurnBet = (EffStack - PotSize)/3.
// Available as a value-betting turn size when stacks are ~<=2x pot; wiring it into
// the turn value line (RaiseBy <amount> vs RaiseBy <pct>%) is deferred to the
// harmonization pass (mixing amount/pct on one street is awkward). [GG turn geometry]
WHEN PotSize >= f$EffStack RETURN 0 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN (f$EffStack - PotSize) / 3 FORCE

##f$BetPctVsStation##
// VALUE size vs a calling station. Counter-intuitively BIGGER, not smaller: a station
// pays off on its own hand strength and reads a big bet as a bluff. Bet ~pot with a
// strong made hand for max value; even overbet on "bingo" boards. [CtM p147,149]
WHEN Others RETURN 100 FORCE

##f$CbetFreqBase##
// How often we fire a continuation bet with air as the pre-flop raiser. [B ~90%][N ~60%]
// [T] TAO of Poker (Phillips) Ch.6 & Ch.14: in loose low-limit fields (our freerolls)
// bluffing into calling stations just donates -- "you still have to win once in a while."
// So the hybrid air c-bet is dialed DOWN (0.72 -> 0.60): bluff less, value-bet more. (The
// bot already CHECKS air vs an identified station in 50_flop -- f$Opp_IsStation Check.)
// Heads-up: c-bet ~80% of missed flops (tiny pots, villain whiffs too) UNLESS a station.
// [HUM p49][HUSNG p11]. Power c-bet capped 0.90 -> 0.80 (the >80% over-bluff leak). [DFR p127]
// PHILOSOPHY: the dialed-DOWN bluff frequency is restraint, not timidity - over-bluffing
// is forcing. [Tao ch.9 "fill a cup to its brim and it spills"][Tao ch.24 "he who strides
// cannot keep pace"][48L L16 "use absence to increase respect" - don't over-bluff].
//
// AGGRESSOR-KNOB MODULATION [Emrald 2026-06-20]: the cross-street rhythm (12_aggressor)
// retunes the air-c-bet frequency. f$AggressorKnob is the PFR=aggressor by definition
// on the flop, so it reads 2 in position / 1 OOP whenever we c-bet; f$ConservativeKnob
// reads >0 only when an OPPONENT is the carried aggressor (i.e. we are NOT the flop PFR,
// so the air-c-bet branches below cannot fire then anyway) - it is wired here for the
// post-flop streets that also call f$CbetFreq (turn float / stab) where we may NOT hold
// the lead. Net effect: fire MORE when pressing in position (knob 2), LESS / give up when
// out of position vs an opp-aggressor in a sticky spot. The f$Style base is preserved.
// [CtM p130 cbet ~75% as the aggressor; p153 give up when they fight back]
WHEN f$ConservativeKnob >= 2 RETURN 0.30 FORCE
WHEN f$ConservativeKnob = 1 RETURN 0.45 FORCE
WHEN f$AggressorKnob >= 2 AND f$HeadsUpPot AND NOT f$Opp_IsStation RETURN 0.88 FORCE
WHEN f$AggressorKnob >= 2 RETURN 0.78 FORCE
WHEN f$HeadsUpPot AND NOT f$Opp_IsStation RETURN 0.80 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 1 RETURN 0.80 FORCE
WHEN f$Style = 0 RETURN 0.60 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.60 FORCE

##f$CbetFreq##
// The c-bet frequency actually used by the street files.
// DIRECT OVERRIDE [Emrald]: the C-bet Frequency knob (Synapse tab) wins when set -- openai_knob_cbet
// = -1 means AUTO (compute below); 0..1 forces exactly that c-bet frequency.
// AUTO = the book/style/rhythm base (f$CbetFreqBase) scaled by the runtime AGGRESSION knob
// (f$AggroFreqMult), clamped so we never c-bet 100% (stays deceptive). Knob neutral (0.5) -> x1.0.
WHEN openai_knob_cbet >= 0 RETURN openai_knob_cbet FORCE
WHEN f$CbetFreqBase * f$AggroFreqMult >= 0.95 RETURN 0.95 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$CbetFreqBase * f$AggroFreqMult FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Draw / pot-odds thresholds.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$CheapDraw##
// The price to continue is small relative to the pot (<= ~25%): call draws.
WHEN AmountToCall * 4 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$DecentPrice##
// A reasonable price to continue (<= ~33% of pot).
WHEN AmountToCall * 3 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$WithinSpecRisk##
// We risk no more than ~10% of our stack on a speculative "bust 'em" call
// (suited connectors / steal equity vs a raise). [N pp.29-30][B S8.6]
// NOTE: this is a COMMITMENT-threshold (10% of stack), NOT the set-mine implied-odds
// test - for pure set-mining use f$SetMineOK below. [SSNL commitment-threshold]
WHEN AmountToCall * 10 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  TIER-1 BOOK EXPANSION (2026-06-15) - dials distilled from the wider NLHE
//  library and reconciled with the [N]/[B]/[T] spine. New source tags:
//    [HoH] Harrington on Hold'em I-II   [KE] Kill Everyone / [KP] Kill Phil
//    [SSNL] Small Stakes No-Limit (Miller/Mehta/Flynn)   [ToP] Theory of Poker
//    [SM] Hold'em for Advanced Players  [CtM] Crushing the Microstakes
//    [PMM] Poker Math That Matters      [MoH] Math of Hold'em
//    [SNG] SNG Blueprint / Moshman / Shaw   [EM] Ed Miller / [TN] Tri Nguyen
//  UNITS: PotSize / StackSize / AmountToCall / f$EffStack are all in BIG BLINDS
//  (OpenPPL divides each by bblind). So SPR = EffStack/PotSize directly; M is a
//  dimensionless ratio. bblind/sblind/ante are the raw chip denominators.
//=============================================================================

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  M-ratio (Magriel/Harrington) - the antes-aware depth measure. M = stack /
//  cost-of-one-orbit (SB+BB+all antes). With antes live, M is materially smaller
//  than the raw bb-depth, so push/fold should kick in earlier. [HoH2 p124-131]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$AnteTotal##
// Total antes posted per orbit, in CHIPS (per-player ante * players dealt).
// 0 when there are no antes; degrades M gracefully to a blinds-only ratio.
// tgi_ante comes from table_game_info (set via the lobby / set_table_game_info).
WHEN Others RETURN tgi_ante * nplayersdealt FORCE

##f$M##
// Harrington M = effective stack / cost per round. f$EffStack is in bb, so
// (f$EffStack * bblind) is chips; divide by the chip cost of one orbit. Ratio.
WHEN (bblind + sblind + f$AnteTotal) <= 0 RETURN 999 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN (f$EffStack * bblind) / (bblind + sblind + f$AnteTotal) FORCE

##f$Mzone##
// 4=Green(M>20) 3=Yellow(10-20) 2=Orange(6-10) 1=Red(1-5) 0=Dead(<1). [HoH2 p128-131]
WHEN f$M > 20 RETURN 4 FORCE
WHEN f$M >= 10 RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$M >= 6  RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$M >= 1  RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others    RETURN 0 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  SPR (stack-to-pot ratio) & commitment. Refines the spine's "don't go broke
//  with one pair" into the HIGH-SPR case: at LOW SPR you SHOULD stack off top
//  pair / overpair. [SSNL SPR sidebar]
//  "Don't go broke with one pair" = knowing when to stop. [Tao ch.44 "know when to
//  stop and you will avoid danger"][48L L35 "master the art of timing"][Prince
//  "virtu/fortuna" -> seize the +EV get-it-in, cap the variance off it].
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$SPR##
// Effective remaining stack / current pot (both already in bb).
WHEN PotSize <= 0 RETURN 999 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$EffStack / PotSize FORCE

##f$Committed##
// Low SPR => stack off top-pair/overpair. Hand-class-specific SPR bands from [PNL p182-186]
// (the source text of the SPR/commitment framework, refining the Tier-1 SSNL approximation):
// overpairs commit at a higher SPR than top pair; aggro opp & wet boards raise the band,
// tight/passive opp lowers it. Multiway (>2): never auto-commit one pair - SPR is measured
// vs the shortest covering stack only. Gate the get-it-in line on this; gate the
// "never go broke with one pair" pot-control on NOT f$Committed. [PNL p182-186][SSNL]
WHEN nopponentsplaying > 2 RETURN false FORCE
WHEN f$SPR <= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveOverPair AND f$Opp_IsAggro AND f$SPR <= 10 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveOverPair AND f$BoardWet AND f$SPR <= 8 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveOverPair AND f$Opp_IsPassive AND f$SPR <= 4 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveOverPair AND f$SPR <= 6 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveTopPair AND f$Opp_IsAggro AND f$SPR <= 7 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveTopPair AND f$BoardWet AND f$SPR <= 6 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveTopPair AND f$Opp_IsPassive AND f$SPR <= 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveTopPair AND f$SPR <= 4 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$SPR <= 3 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Exact pot-odds & set-mining implied-odds (replaces the coarse K-bucket
//  helpers for the cases that want precision). [PMM p59-63][MoH][SSNL p143]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$RequiredEquity##
// Win% needed to call = call / (pot-before-our-call + call). Compare vs prwin.
WHEN (PotSize + AmountToCall) <= 0 RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN AmountToCall / (PotSize + AmountToCall) FORCE

##f$SetMineOK##
// Set-mine a small pair only with enough effective stack behind for real implied odds.
// Tiered: loose/station pay off (15x ok); regs/foldy need more (~22x); full-ring deeper
// than 6-max (20x vs 15x); never vs a nit. [CtM p122 15x][PMM 15x][DFR p41 20x FR][HC p148 ~25x tight]
//
// MTT MID/LATE-STAGE GUARD: in a TOURNAMENT, once we are out of the early stage
// (f$Stage>=1: short, 6-max-deep, bubble or ITM) OR the effective stack is shallow
// (<=30bb), the 10-to-1 implied odds set-mining needs simply are not there - the pot
// can't grow enough and squeeze-risk behind is high. Require a much deeper ~25x, else
// fold. CASH is unchanged (tgi_players_remaining is 0/unknown off-tournament, so this
// guard never fires). [WPT2 "set-mining is out of the question at THIS stage"]
WHEN f$Opp_IsNit RETURN false FORCE
WHEN tgi_players_remaining >= 2 AND (f$Stage >= 1 OR f$EffStack <= 30) AND AmountToCall * 25 > f$EffStack RETURN false FORCE
WHEN (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsLoose) AND AmountToCall * 15 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN (f$Opp_IsTAG OR f$Opp_Foldy) AND AmountToCall * 22 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Is6Max AND AmountToCall * 15 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall * 20 <= f$EffStack RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Table size. The open lists are full-ring/8-max shapes; 6-max wants the EP/MP
//  seats to play wider. [V6 charts]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$Is6Max##
WHEN nplayersdealt <= 6 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Tournament STAGE & bubble pressure. Scales the ICM get-it-in margin: tighter
//  near the bubble, looser in the money / heads-up. [SNG][KE p120-126]
//  NOTE: these depend on a REAL lobby payout curve (f$PaidPlaces). The current
//  f$icm_prizeX is a placeholder where all 8 places "pay", so f$NearBubble stays
//  false and f$BubbleTighten stays 1.0 (= today's behavior) until the real payout
//  table is scraped (lobby_fetch -> settings.lobby_info). Structurally ready.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$PaidPlaces##
// Number of paid finishing positions = count of nonzero prizes in the curve.
WHEN f$icm_prize8 > 0 RETURN 8 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize7 > 0 RETURN 7 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize6 > 0 RETURN 6 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize5 > 0 RETURN 5 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize4 > 0 RETURN 4 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize3 > 0 RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$icm_prize2 > 0 RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 1 FORCE

##f$NearBubble##
// One elimination from the money. Uses tgi_players_remaining (tournament-wide
// players left, from the lobby) - 0/unknown for cash, so this stays false there.
WHEN tgi_players_remaining = f$PaidPlaces + 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$InMoney##
WHEN tgi_players_remaining <= f$PaidPlaces AND tgi_players_remaining >= 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HeadsUpTourney##
// Two players left in the tournament: ICM is off, chips become linear money. [SoS p94]
WHEN tgi_players_remaining = 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Stage##
// 0 early  1 middle  2 bubble  3 ITM/HU
WHEN f$HeadsUpTourney OR f$InMoney RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$NearBubble RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$ShortStack OR nplayersdealt <= 6 RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

##f$BubbleTighten##
// Required $-equity edge over folding when getting it in. >1 = need more, near
// the bubble; <1 = gamble looser in the money. [SNG][KE p120]
WHEN f$Stage = 2 RETURN 1.06 FORCE
WHEN f$Stage = 3 RETURN 0.97 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 1.00 FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  TIER-2 WAVE-1 dials (cash/MTT/SNG/HU library). Engine-native symbols only.
//    [PNL][HC][EG][ER][LTBR][ASH][JL][RE][SNF][W][SYS][NSS][HUM][HUSNG][DFR][RF]
//=============================================================================

##f$Open_RaiseTo_HU##
// Heads-up button/SB open size: minraise when short, 2.5bb deeper. [HUM p51][HUSNG p37]
WHEN f$EffStack <= 25 RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 2.5 FORCE

##f$ReshoveSpot##
// 3-bet-JAM over a single open in the ~16-25bb band - the fold-equity re-steal the
// push/fold tree misses (too deep to open-jam, too short to flat-and-play). Fires only
// over exactly one raise, in/near position or the blinds, vs a wide opener. [JL p1161][RE p2280]
// Win the pot uncontested - subdue the enemy without fighting. [SunTzu III.2 "supreme
// excellence is to subdue the enemy without fighting"][48L L28 "enter action with boldness"].
// NOT f$PushFoldStack makes the band genuinely DISJOINT from push/fold: on an ante table
// the Red-zone M<=5 trigger can push the jam regime above 15bb, so the raw 15<EffStack<=25
// window would otherwise overlap it. The push/fold tree (open-jam, ICM call) owns that case;
// this re-steal owns only the truly-deeper 16-25bb spots. Honors the "no gap or overlap"
// handoff invariant in the dial itself, not just by f$preflop dispatch order. [HoH2 p140]
WHEN f$PushFoldStack RETURN false FORCE
WHEN Raises = 1 AND f$EffStack > 15 AND f$EffStack <= 25 AND (f$Opp_IsLoose OR f$Opp_IsAggro) AND (InButton OR InCutOff OR InSmallBlind OR InBigBlind) AND listReshove RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$DoubleBarrel##
// Fire a 2nd barrel as the flop aggressor: vs reg/foldy types (NEVER stations/fish),
// heads-up, on a scary or dry board that missed villain's peeling range; suppress when
// way behind on a wet board. The turn is an under-bet street. [EG p52][ER p8][LTBR p14][ASH p61]
// Never barrel a POT-COMMITTED / cornered villain (no fold equity). [SunTzu VII.36 "leave a
// golden bridge for a retreating army"][SunTzu IV "do not attack his strength" vs station/fish]
WHEN f$Opp_PotCommitted RETURN false FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish RETURN false FORCE
WHEN NOT (f$WasPreflopRaiser AND BotRaisedOnFlop AND f$HeadsUpPot) RETURN false FORCE
WHEN StraightPossible AND prwin < 0.50 RETURN false FORCE
WHEN (f$ScaryBoard OR f$BoardDry) AND f$Opp_Foldy RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ThreeBetBluffFreqBase##
// Frequency cap for 3-bet bluffs by opponent type: bluff foldy/nits often (they over-fold),
// never stations/fish or light-3-bettors (no fold equity / they fight back). [ER p7][LTBR p11]
// [SunTzu VI.30 "attack where he is unprepared, undefended" -> attack fold equity (foldy/nit
// high)][SunTzu IV "first make yourself invincible; do not attack his strength" -> 0 vs
// stations/fish, value-bet that instead][Prince "feared > loved" -> exploit the foldy image].
// Never bluff a POT-COMMITTED / cornered villain who cannot fold (no fold equity). [SunTzu
// VII.36 "leave a golden bridge for a retreating army"][Tao ch.69 "no greater disaster than
// underestimating the enemy"].
WHEN f$Opp_PotCommitted RETURN 0 FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish RETURN 0 FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_ThreeBetsLight RETURN 0 FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_IsNit RETURN 0.70 FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_Foldy RETURN 0.55 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.30 FORCE

##f$ThreeBetBluffFreq##
// The 3-bet-bluff frequency used by 40_preflop = the opponent-typed base scaled by the runtime
// BLUFF knob (f$BluffFreqMult). Capped at 0.90 so we never 3-bet-bluff a foldy type 100%. Vs
// stations/fish/light-3bettors/pot-committed the base is already 0 -> stays 0 (knob can't create
// fold equity that isn't there). Knob neutral -> unchanged. [Emrald bluff knob]
WHEN f$ThreeBetBluffFreqBase * f$BluffFreqMult >= 0.90 RETURN 0.90 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$ThreeBetBluffFreqBase * f$BluffFreqMult FORCE

##f$DoubleBarrelFreq##
// Turn double-barrel bluff frequency (base 0.62) scaled by the runtime BLUFF knob. [Emrald]
WHEN 0.62 * f$BluffFreqMult >= 0.95 RETURN 0.95 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.62 * f$BluffFreqMult FORCE

##f$TripleBarrelFreq##
// River triple-barrel bluff frequency (base 0.22, kept deliberately LOW) scaled by the BLUFF knob.
WHEN 0.22 * f$BluffFreqMult >= 0.60 RETURN 0.60 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.22 * f$BluffFreqMult FORCE

##f$FloatStabFreq##
// In-position flop stab/float frequency (base 0.50) scaled by the BLUFF knob.
WHEN 0.50 * f$BluffFreqMult >= 0.90 RETURN 0.90 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.50 * f$BluffFreqMult FORCE

##f$FloatTurnFreq##
// Float-the-turn take-away frequency (base 0.70) scaled by the BLUFF knob.
WHEN 0.70 * f$BluffFreqMult >= 0.95 RETURN 0.95 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.70 * f$BluffFreqMult FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Bet-timing tells.  Hiss measures how long each chair dwells on its to-act
//  highlight (pNactive rect1) and exposes lastraiseractiontime = the seconds the
//  player we must react to took on his bet/raise. Classic Caro/Negreanu reads:
//  a SNAP (instant) bet leans weak/automatic; a long TANK then a bet leans strong.
//  Reads are noisy, so they are used only as soft modifiers, only heads-up, only
//  when a reading exists. Set f$UseTimingTells = 0 to disable entirely.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$UseTimingTells##
WHEN Others RETURN 1 FORCE

##f$SnapSeconds##
// At or below this, the bet was effectively instant.
WHEN Others RETURN 1.5 FORCE

##f$TankSeconds##
// At or above this, the player tanked before betting.
WHEN Others RETURN 6 FORCE

##f$TimingKnown##
// A sane, fresh reading exists for the player we are reacting to.
WHEN f$UseTimingTells = 0 RETURN false FORCE
WHEN lastraiseractiontime > 0 AND lastraiseractiontime < 90 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$TimingSaysWeak##
// Snap bet/raise, heads-up: lean toward it being weak/automatic. (Caro: a fast
// bet is often a weak bet.) Continue/bluff-catch a touch wider against it.
WHEN f$TimingKnown AND f$HeadsUpPot AND lastraiseractiontime <= f$SnapSeconds RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$TimingSaysStrong##
// Long tank then a bet/raise, heads-up: lean toward genuine strength. Fold the
// marginal hands we would otherwise pay off; do not bluff-raise into it.
WHEN f$TimingKnown AND f$HeadsUpPot AND lastraiseractiontime >= f$TankSeconds RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ICM (Independent Chip Model).  The engine's CSymbolEngineICM computes our
//  TOURNAMENT-$ equity for each line (icm_fold / icm_callwin / icm_calllose)
//  from the live table stacks + the payout structure below. We use it for the
//  short-stack get-it-in decision so calls/jams are $-correct, not just chip-EV
//  (survival has value when the payouts are top-heavy). [tournament]
//
//  f$icm_prizeX = fraction of the prize pool paid for finishing Xth AT THE TABLE
//  (a final-table approximation). Sum must = 1.00. This is a standard top-heavy
//  8-max curve; replace with the real lobby payout table once scraped.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$icm_prize1##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.300 FORCE
##f$icm_prize2##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.220 FORCE
##f$icm_prize3##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.160 FORCE
##f$icm_prize4##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.120 FORCE
##f$icm_prize5##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.085 FORCE
##f$icm_prize6##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.060 FORCE
##f$icm_prize7##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.035 FORCE
##f$icm_prize8##
WHEN Others RETURN 0.020 FORCE

##f$ICM_CallEV##
// Tournament-$ EV of CALLING an all-in = P(win)*equity-if-win + P(lose)*equity-if-lose.
// (Ties are rare in an all-in and folded into the win/lose split.) icm_callwin /
// icm_calllose are the ICM equities of the resulting stacks from CSymbolEngineICM.
WHEN Others RETURN prwin * icm_callwin + (1 - prwin) * icm_calllose FORCE

##f$ICM_CallShove##
// CASH GAME: ICM is meaningless (a chip = its cash value), and evaluating icm_* makes the engine's
// prize-sum validator pop "Incorrect f$icm_prizeX-functions ... 0.000" (prizes are 0 in cash). Return
// false FIRST so icm_* is never touched in cash; cash get-it-in falls to the chip-EV listCallShove floor.
WHEN NOT istournament RETURN false FORCE
// Is getting it in $-correct? Call/jam when the ICM EV of calling beats folding,
// scaled by the bubble factor: near the bubble we need a real edge (survival has
// value); in the money / heads-up we gamble looser. f$BubbleTighten is 1.0 until a
// real payout curve is scraped, so this matches today's behavior. [SNG][KE p120]
WHEN f$HeadsUpTourney AND f$ICM_CallEV >= icm_fold RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$ICM_CallEV >= icm_fold * f$BubbleTighten RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  ICM bet-SIZING multiplier. Scales every OHF open/iso/3bet/4bet (RaiseTo) and
//  post-flop bet (RaiseBy %) by the ICM CHIP VALUE: in a tournament the chips you
//  can LOSE are worth more than the chips you can WIN (concave ICM curve), most
//  acutely near/in the money -> bet a touch SMALLER to risk fewer of your dear
//  chips while still applying fold pressure. Far from the money / in CASH a chip
//  ~ its face value -> full size (1.0). Lobby-fed: f$Stage uses tgi_players_remaining
//  + the payout curve, so this sharpens automatically as the field shrinks. Returns
//  1.0 (no change) for cash, freerolls, and early/middle play, so it is inert until
//  a real money tournament reaches the bubble. Jams (push/fold all-in) are sized by
//  the autoplayer's RaiseMax, not these functions, so survival jams are untouched.
//  [Emrald: "the betsizes in OHF bets should be relative to the ICM CHIP VALUE"]
##f$ICM_SizeMult##
WHEN NOT istournament RETURN 1.000 FORCE
WHEN f$HeadsUpTourney RETURN 1.000 FORCE
WHEN f$Stage = 2 RETURN 0.80 FORCE
WHEN f$Stage = 3 RETURN 0.90 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 1.000 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  STACK-DEPTH-PROPORTIONAL sizing (leverage). A fixed bb bet is nothing to a very deep stack and
//  everything to a short one [Emrald], so scale every bet/raise to the EFFECTIVE stack depth (f$EffStack,
//  in bb -- the stack actually at risk this hand, capped at the opponent). DEEP -> size UP so bets keep
//  fold equity and build pots worth the deep stacks; SHORT -> the push/fold tree owns commitment (jam),
//  so don't scale there. Capped at 1.5x so it never balloons. This is bet sizing relative to stack depth
//  (SPR / leverage / effective-stack-proportional sizing).
##f$DepthSizeMult##
WHEN f$EffStack <= 25 RETURN 1.00 FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack >= 250 RETURN 1.50 FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack >= 150 RETURN 1.35 FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack >= 100 RETURN 1.20 FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack >= 60 RETURN 1.10 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 1.00 FORCE

//  Combined bet-size multiplier applied to every OHF open/iso/3bet/4bet (RaiseTo) and post-flop bet
//  (RaiseBy %): ICM chip value x stack-depth proportionality.
##f$SizeMult##
WHEN Others RETURN f$ICM_SizeMult * f$DepthSizeMult FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  10_opponents - opponent model from the PokerTracker HUD stats.
//  Both books insist you "play the opponent's hand, not your own" [N P1][B P7.1]
//  and that you adjust to player TYPE (tight/loose/station/aggressive). A bot
//  cannot read physical tells or table image, but it CAN read aggregated stats,
//  so this is our machine-observable substitute. Stats describe the LAST RAISER
//  (the player we must react to) and default to neutral when the sample is thin.
//
//  PHILOSOPHY: opponent typing + own M/stack/SPR awareness (05_config) IS the
//  oldest maxim of the craft. [SunTzu III.18 "know the enemy and know yourself,
//  and in a hundred battles you will never be in peril"][Prince "adapt to the
//  times" -> the whole archetype set + the depth/M regimes][48L L15 "crush your
//  enemy totally" -> value-big vs the weak (f$BetPctVsStation)].
//*****************************************************************************

##f$Opp_Hands##
pt_hands_raischair

##f$Opp_Known##
// Trust a read only with a meaningful sample.
WHEN f$Opp_Hands >= 30 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_VPIP##
WHEN f$Opp_Known RETURN pt_vpip_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 25 FORCE

##f$Opp_PFR##
WHEN f$Opp_Known RETURN pt_pfr_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 18 FORCE

##f$Opp_AF##
WHEN f$Opp_Known RETURN pt_flop_af_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 2 FORCE

##f$Opp_WTSD##
WHEN f$Opp_Known RETURN pt_wtsd_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 28 FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Player archetypes -> map to the books' adjustments.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$Opp_IsNit##
// Tight: their raises mean strength -> respect them; 3-bet-bluff/steal more. [N p.30][B B9.5]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP < 17 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsLoose##
// Wide opener -> isolate / value 3-bet wider. [N p.19]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP > 32 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsStation##
// Calls down too much -> value-bet thin & BIG, NEVER bluff. [N p.158][B B9.3]
// Broadened to catch the canonical passive fish (very high VPIP, very low PFR,
// low aggression) even before WTSD has a sample. [CtM p40][TN p15][EM]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_WTSD > 34 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_AF < 1.0 AND f$Opp_VPIP > 40 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP > 35 AND f$Opp_PFR < 10 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_AF < 1.5 AND f$Opp_VPIP > 32 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsPassive##
// Low aggression -> their bets/raises mean a real hand. [N]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_AF < 1.3 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsAggro##
// High aggression / will barrel & bluff -> induce, trap, bluff-catch wider. [N p.53]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_AF > 3.0 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_ThreeBetsLight##
// Reraises light (3-bets far more than he value-opens) -> just call, don't 3-bet
// into him; flat JJ/QQ/AK and outplay post-flop. [N p.22]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND (f$Opp_PFR - f$Opp_VPIP) > -4 AND f$Opp_PFR > 22 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_Foldy##
// Folds a lot pre/post -> our c-bets and steals print money. [B R1.2]
WHEN f$Opp_IsNit RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_WTSD < 24 AND f$Opp_VPIP < 22 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Additional archetypes from the wider library. The originals lumped these in:
//  f$Opp_IsAggro fired on AF alone (a TIGHT-aggressive nit counts), which is the
//  wrong read for a LAG. These split the population out cleanly. [EM PtP][TN][CtM]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$Opp_IsFish##
// Pure recreational: very loose + very passive. Value-bet relentlessly & big,
// keep pots small pre (flat premiums, don't 3-bet), never bluff. [CtM p40][EM HRH]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP > 40 AND f$Opp_PFR < 8 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsTAG##
// Tight-aggressive REG: opens then bet-folds; floats/raises print vs his c-bets,
// but pay off his committing bets. The original model had no TAG branch. [EM PtP p274]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP >= 18 AND f$Opp_VPIP <= 26 AND (f$Opp_VPIP - f$Opp_PFR) < 6 AND f$Opp_AF >= 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsLAG##
// Loose-AND-aggressive: 3-bets & barrels wide. Deny info (call down, don't raise
// to "find out"); widen our own calling/3-bet ranges. [EM PtP p677]
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP > 28 AND f$Opp_PFR > 20 AND f$Opp_AF > 2.5 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsManiac##
// Hyper-aggressive, no fold equity against him: trap & induce, never bluff. [CtM p41]
// CtM stat profile: VPIP very high, PFR very high, AF very high, fold-to-cbet very low.
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP > 45 AND f$Opp_PFR > 30 AND f$Opp_AF > 4 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_IsSLP##
// SEMI-LOOSE-PASSIVE - BlackRain79's distinct micro archetype the model was
// missing: a casual player who plays too many hands but passively (~24/6, low AF).
// He calls too much and calls any draw, but is NOT the 40%+ pure fish. The play vs
// him is the same family as the fish: VALUE-BET WIDE & relentlessly, do NOT bluff
// (low fold equity), pot-control thin. Sits between f$Opp_IsLoose and f$Opp_IsFish:
// looser/wider than the fish floor but with the same passive, station-like calling
// pattern. [CtM p38 "SLPs - value bet frequently and with a fairly wide range";
// p169 "barrel SLPs and fish for value"; p176 "don't bluff SLPs and fish"]
WHEN f$Opp_IsFish RETURN false FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_Known AND f$Opp_VPIP >= 20 AND f$Opp_VPIP <= 40 AND f$Opp_PFR < 10 AND f$Opp_AF < 1.5 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  MICRO-STAKES BET-PATTERN reads (BlackRain79's "fish psychology"). At the
//  micros the population is so face-up that the SIZE/SHAPE of villain's bet leaks
//  his strength directly - independent of his archetype. These feed f$OppRepresents
//  (12_aggressor) and the street value/bluff gates.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$Opp_MinBetLead##
// A min-ish lead/probe bet (<= ~1.5bb, or <= ~20% pot): "seeing where they're at."
// A dead giveaway of a weak/capped range (draw, weak pair, air) and very often a
// recreational player. Ignore it / treat as a check and bet our standard size; raise
// it wide IP for value or as a semibluff. NEVER fold a real hand to it. [CtM p232
// "min bets - just pretend they checked"; p150 donk; p210-211 probe bets]
WHEN AmountToCall <= 0 RETURN false FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall <= 1.5 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall * 5 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_NutsyRaise##
// A TURN or RIVER raise (we bet, villain raised) - at the micros this is "always
// the nuts": two pair or better. Fold one pair / overpairs a lot, never bluff-raise
// back. Flop raises are NOT included (those can be draws/wide). [CtM p216 "turn
// raises are usually the nuts"; p217 "river raises are ALWAYS the nuts"]
WHEN (IsTurn OR IsRiver) AND Raises >= 1 AND AmountToCall > 0 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Opp_PotCommitted##
// "Do not press a desperate foe" - a villain who CANNOT fold has no fold equity to
// attack, so do not bluff him; value-bet or check instead. The station/fish/maniac
// cases are already bluff-suppressed elsewhere; the NET-NEW piece is the cornered
// SHORT-STACK opponent - an all-in-bound low-M player is pot-committed to anything he
// continues with. Gate bluffs (f$DoubleBarrel, the river triple-barrel, f$ThreeBetBluffFreq)
// on NOT f$Opp_PotCommitted. [SunTzu VII.36 "leave a golden bridge for a retreating army"]
// [Tao ch.69 "no greater disaster than underestimating the enemy"]
WHEN f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsManiac RETURN true FORCE
// SLPs call too much / have no fold equity vs a bluff, just like stations & fish -
// suppress bluffs into them too (value-bet wide instead). [CtM p176 don't bluff SLPs]
WHEN f$Opp_IsSLP RETURN true FORCE
WHEN EffectiveMaxStacksizeOfActiveOpponents <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  BLIND-STEAL exploit: the player typing above describes the RAISER (raischair),
//  which is useless when WE are the one open-stealing (there is no raiser yet). To
//  steal correctly we must read the BLINDS we are attacking. PokerTracker exposes
//  positional stats, so read the SB / BB directly. Confirmed nits in the blinds fold
//  to opens far too often -> open WIDER (listStealNit). [N p.30 "attack the weak-tight"]
//  Observationally learned: observe_learn flagged H1GHJACK / metared as nits.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$BB_Nit##
// DISABLED 2026-06-20: positional PT symbols pt_vpip_bigblind / pt_hands_bigblind are NOT valid in this
// engine (the only valid positional forms end in a recognized "...chair" suffix that translates to a
// numeric chair, e.g. pt_vpip_bigblindchair) and the bad form pops an "Invalid PokerTracker-symbol"
// modal on EVERY evaluation. Inert for now -> f$BlindsAreNitty=false -> normal positional opens.
// TODO: re-enable with a VERIFIED symbol (pt_vpip_bigblindchair) or an /api-pushed blind-nit signal.
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$SB_Nit##
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$BlindsAreNitty##
// From the SB it is heads-up vs the BB, so only the BB matters. From CO/BTN both blinds
// are behind us, so require BOTH foldy (a loose SB would punish an any-two steal).
WHEN InSmallBlind RETURN f$BB_Nit FORCE
WHEN (InButton OR InCutOff) AND f$BB_Nit AND f$SB_Nit RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  11_introspection - the INTUITION layer.
//
//  Harmonizes HUD + per-opponent INTROSPECTION (rhythm / exploits / timing /
//  range, gametype-separated) + the live Claude decision advisor into a single
//  read the strategy decides FROM. The decision files (50/60/70/40/05/12) route
//  through f$Intuition_* / f$Exploit_* below; the raw symbols are just inputs.
//
//  Native engine symbols (defined in the rebuilt binary):
//    intro_* / exploit_*  -> CSymbolEngineOpponentIntrospection (opponent_profile,
//                            built by mcp/introspect_aggregator.py; gametype-matched)
//    openai_knob_advice_*  -> mcp/decision_advisor.py via /api/knob (fresh-only)
//  Villain for "facing a bet" spots = raischair (the current aggressor). The
//  multiplexer resolves intro_contfreq_raischair -> intro_contfreqN automatically.
//*****************************************************************************

// ============================ introspection answers ========================
##f$Intro_Known##
// enough of a sample on THIS villain in THIS gametype to trust the read
WHEN intro_known_raischair >= 1 AND intro_simN_raischair >= 12 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Intro_WillKeepFiring##
// "should I raise him, or will he just fire again?" rhythm 0..1 (-1 unknown)
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND intro_contfreq_raischair >= 0 RETURN intro_contfreq_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN -1 FORCE

##f$Intro_FastTell##
// "he bet quickly - does he have it when he bets fast?"  P(strong|fast) 0..1 (-1 unknown)
WHEN intro_fasttell_raischair >= 0 RETURN intro_fasttell_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN -1 FORCE

##f$Intro_Tilt##
// current EMOTION/steam: how far his recent rhythm has deviated from his baseline (0..1; 0 = on his game)
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND intro_tilt_raischair >= 0 RETURN intro_tilt_raischair FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

// ============================ exploit flags (actionable) ===================
##f$Exploit_Overfold##
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_overfold_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_GivesUp##
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_givesup_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_KeepsFiring##
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_keepsfiring_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_NeverFolds##
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_neverfolds_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_Folds3Bet##
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_folds3bet_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_FastWeak##
WHEN exploit_fastweak_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_FastStrong##
WHEN exploit_faststrong_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_Honest##
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_honest_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Exploit_Tilt##
// villain is STEAMING (off his baseline) -> stop bluffing him, value-bet bigger, bluff-catch wider;
// he'll spew if we just let him. The single highest-EV exploit when it fires.
WHEN f$Intro_Known AND exploit_tilting_raischair >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Intro_Tilt >= 0.35 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

// ============================ table read: DONK-FEST ========================
// A donk-heavy table (3+ fish / stations / loose-passive seated) -> get in CHEAP preflop and value-bet
// HEAVY postflop when we connect; they pay off, so stack up. (intro_donkfest is a table-level symbol.)
##f$Table_DonkFest##
WHEN intro_donkfest >= 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

// ============================ card / range guess ===========================
// 0 = capped / bluffy .. 1 = nutted. Profile prior (engine) refined by the live line. -1 unknown.
##f$Range_VillainStrength##
WHEN intro_rangestrength_raischair < 0 RETURN -1 FORCE
WHEN f$OppMinLead RETURN intro_rangestrength_raischair * 0.5 FORCE
WHEN (IsTurn OR IsRiver) AND Raises >= 1 RETURN intro_rangestrength_raischair * 0.5 + 0.5 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_FastWeak RETURN intro_rangestrength_raischair * 0.6 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_FastStrong RETURN intro_rangestrength_raischair * 0.6 + 0.4 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN intro_rangestrength_raischair FORCE

// ============================ live advisor channels ========================
// fresh-only in the engine (decay to 0 / -1 when the advisor is quiet)
##f$Advice_Conf##
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_advice_conf FORCE
##f$Advice_Raise##
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_advice_raise FORCE
##f$Advice_Bluff##
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_advice_bluff FORCE
##f$Advice_Value##
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_advice_value FORCE
##f$Advice_Fold##
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_advice_fold FORCE
##f$Advice_Persona##
WHEN Others RETURN openai_knob_advice_persona FORCE

// ============================ bot counter-persona ==========================
// The BOT adopts whatever archetype best exploits THIS villain (1 nit..6 maniac; -1 normal).
// Advisor override first, else infer the nightmare matchup from the villain's exploit profile.
##f$BotPersona##
WHEN f$Advice_Persona >= 0 RETURN f$Advice_Persona FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_NeverFolds RETURN 2 FORCE                              // station/fish -> tight VALUE (tag)
WHEN f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_Folds3Bet RETURN 6 FORCE        // folds too much -> MANIAC pressure
WHEN f$Exploit_KeepsFiring RETURN 4 FORCE                            // chronic bettor -> STATION, snap him off
WHEN Others RETURN -1 FORCE

// ============================ INTUITION (the spine) ========================
// One harmonized read. Decisions are made FROM these, not from the raw inputs.

##f$Intuition_VillainStrength##
// unified estimate of the villain's range/holding strength now (0..1; -1 unknown)
WHEN f$Range_VillainStrength >= 0 RETURN f$Range_VillainStrength FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN -1 FORCE

##f$Intuition_Confidence##
// how much to trust the intuition (0..1): advisor confidence, else introspection sample weight
WHEN f$Advice_Conf > 0 RETURN f$Advice_Conf FORCE
WHEN f$Intro_Known RETURN 0.6 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.2 FORCE

##f$Intuition_Aggression##
// how aggressive WE should be (0.5 neutral): style knob + advisor raise/bluff lean (weighted by
// advisor confidence) + a push toward attacking foldable villains / restraint vs sticky ones.
WHEN f$Exploit_NeverFolds AND f$Range_VillainStrength >= 0.6 RETURN 0.2 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_Tilt RETURN 0.72 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp RETURN 0.75 + f$Advice_Raise * f$Advice_Conf * 0.2 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0.5 + (openai_knob_aggro - 0.5) * 0.5 + f$Advice_Raise * f$Advice_Conf * 0.3 + f$Advice_Bluff * f$Advice_Conf * 0.2 FORCE

##f$Intuition_Exploit##
// the dominant exploit to act on: 1 barrel/bluff, 2 value-only, 3 bluff-catch/don't-bluff,
// 4 attack-fast-bet, 5 respect (fast=strong/honest), 0 none.
WHEN f$Exploit_Tilt RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_NeverFolds RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_KeepsFiring RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_FastStrong OR f$Exploit_Honest RETURN 5 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp OR f$Exploit_Folds3Bet RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_FastWeak RETURN 4 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

##f$Intuition_ShowOfForce##
// We're ATTACHED to the chips (considerable investment / committed) AND a big bet or jam is the best
// way to WIN the pot now -- fold equity vs this villain + denial make the show of force +EV.
WHEN (f$Committed OR PotSize >= 12 * bblind) AND (f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_Folds3Bet OR intro_foldpress_raischair > 0.5) RETURN true FORCE
WHEN (f$Committed OR PotSize >= 12 * bblind) AND f$Range_VillainStrength >= 0 AND f$Range_VillainStrength < 0.4 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

// ============================ OBSERVER STRATEGY GOTO (Phase 2) =====================================
// obsbranch (1..7, set by observer_strategy.py via /api/knob, engine-fresh-gated to 0 when the brain is
// quiet) is the table-wide PLAN selector. Its aggro/bluff/openrange targets already STEER the OHF
// frequencies (f$AggroFreqMult / f$BluffFreqMult / f$OpenRangeKnob in 05_config) -- VALUE_STATION pushes
// obsbranch_bluff low so we stop bluffing the station, ATTACK_FOLDERS pushes aggro high. f$ObsStrategy
// is the GOTO dispatch hook (today a -1 fall-through -> no forced-action / action-constant pitfalls).
##f$ObsBranch##
WHEN Others RETURN obsbranch FORCE

##f$ObsStrategy##
WHEN Others RETURN -1 FORCE

// ============================ BRAIN-ACTION soft pre-empt (Phase 2) =================================
// The synapse current_decided_action, pushed as brain_action_kind (1 fold / 2 check / 3 call / 4 raise)
// + brain_action_conf + brain_action_size_bb. f$BrainAction maps it to a concrete action; the street
// dispatchers gate it on conf >= 0.60 so a stale / low-confidence push never steers. DISABLED by default
// -- the Python pushes brain_action only when explicitly enabled, exactly like the openai_action hijack.
##f$BrainAction##
WHEN brain_action_kind = 4 RETURN brain_action_size_bb FORCE
WHEN brain_action_kind = 3 Call FORCE
WHEN brain_action_kind = 2 Check FORCE
WHEN brain_action_kind = 1 Fold FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN -1 FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  12_aggressor - CROSS-STREET AGGRESSOR RHYTHM + "what is the opponent
//  representing" inference.  [Emrald 2026-06-20]
//
//  Two engine symbols, REMEMBERED across the current + previous street, drive
//  this whole file (added to the C++ engine + the lint whitelist):
//     aggressorchair  chair 0-9 of the last raiser (-1 = none yet this hand)
//     iamaggressor    1 if aggressorchair = userchair, else 0
//
//  The two ideas here are the micro-stakes spine made explicit:
//   1) RHYTHM. When the OPPONENT is the aggressor and I act before him next
//      street (out of position vs him), the +EV play is to LET HIM DO THE
//      BETTING - check, call raises with good-but-not-monster hands, and tighten
//      bluffs - rather than lead/bet into the player who has the initiative.
//      When *I* am the aggressor, keep barreling good equity / fold-equity spots.
//      [CtM p153-174 "give up when they fight back"; p166 "when you've shown all
//      this aggression and still can't shake them, you are usually behind";
//      p59 "the importance of position" - OOP you play the hand blind].
//   2) STORY. The opponent's BETTING LINE represents a perceived range. At the
//      micros the population is so face-up (passive, unbalanced) that the line
//      itself tells you whether to ATTACK, call, or RESPECT. [EM "How to Read
//      Hands" / "Playing the Player" - read the line, not the cards][CtM
//      "perceived ranges" p132, "turn/river raises are the nuts" p216-217].
//
//  These dials are CONSUMED by 50_flop / 60_turn / 70_river / 05_config
//  (f$CbetFreq). They are additive soft modifiers reconciled with the existing
//  spine - they tighten/loosen at the margin, they do not double-fire the value
//  or commitment lines.
//*****************************************************************************

//=============================================================================
//  (1)  CROSS-STREET AGGRESSOR RHYTHM
//=============================================================================

##f$IAmAggressor##
// I hold the betting initiative carried across streets (I made the last raise).
iamaggressor

##f$AggressorIsOpp##
// An opponent holds the initiative (someone has raised this hand and it is not me).
WHEN aggressorchair >= 0 AND NOT iamaggressor RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ActBeforeAggressor##
// I act before the aggressor on the next street, i.e. I am OUT OF POSITION vs the
// player who holds the initiative. This is the "let THEM do the betting, call
// raises with good hands" rhythm spot: betting into the aggressor OOP bloats the
// pot blind and folds out everything I beat. [CtM p59 position][EM read-the-line]
WHEN f$AggressorIsOpp AND NOT f$InPositionPost RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ConservativeKnob##
// 0/1/2 restraint dial. UP a LOT (2) when I am OOP vs an opponent-aggressor
// (f$ActBeforeAggressor) - this is the highest-discipline rhythm spot (check &
// call, don't lead, tighten bluffs); UP SOME (1) when an opponent merely holds
// the initiative but I have position on him; 0 otherwise. [CtM "give up when they
// fight back"][Tao ch.78 "the soft and yielding overcomes"]
WHEN f$ActBeforeAggressor RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$AggressorIsOpp RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

##f$AggressorKnob##
// 0/1/2 pressure dial. UP a LOT (2) when I am the aggressor AND in position
// (keep barreling - position + initiative is the whole edge); UP SOME (1) when I
// am the aggressor out of position; 0 when I do not hold the initiative.
// [CtM p56 "the importance of initiative"; p130 cbet ~75%]
WHEN f$IAmAggressor AND f$InPositionPost RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$IAmAggressor RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  (2)  "WHAT IS THE OPPONENT REPRESENTING" - story / perceived-range inference
//
//  Scale (gates value / bluff / fold downstream):
//    0  NO STORY      - checked to me / no aggression yet -> normal lines.
//    1  CAPPED / WEAK  - a line that caps the range: a small donk/min-lead, a
//       float (flat) line, or a STATION/FISH who bets (no real range - they bet
//       any pair/draw). -> ATTACK: bluff-raise / float / thin value widened.
//       [CtM p150 "donked into" raise wide; p210-211 "min/donk/probe bets are a
//       dead giveaway they have nothing"; p162 float = hit but not huge].
//    2  MERGED / STD   - one standard c-bet / single barrel. -> call good, fold
//       air. The default postflop story. [CtM p131 cbetting; p153 after the cbet].
//    3  STRONG / CREDIBLE - a credible nut-weighted line: a 3-bet+ preflop line,
//       a check-raise, a TURN or RIVER raise/lead, a NIT/PASSIVE player firing,
//       or a pot-committed villain on a scary/coordinated board. -> RESPECT:
//       fold marginal, NO bluff-raise. [CtM p216 "turn raises are the nuts";
//       p217 "river raises are ALWAYS the nuts"; p153 "passive players raising =
//       strength"; p202 "facing aggression with an overpair - fold vs nits"]
//=============================================================================

##f$OppCheckedToMe##
// No villain aggression on THIS street: it is checked to me (no bet to call and
// no raise this round). The story is "0 - no story" foundation.
WHEN AmountToCall = 0 AND Bets = 0 AND Raises = 0 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$OppMinLead##
// A tiny donk/probe lead (<= ~30% pot) facing us: at the micros this caps the
// villain hard - "they want to see where they are at"; it is a draw / weak pair /
// air far more than a value bet. Treat as weakness to attack. [CtM p150,p210-211]
WHEN AmountToCall > 0 AND AmountToCall * 3 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$OppCheckedPriorStreet##
// The opponent showed weakness earlier in the hand: there was no villain bet or
// raise on a PREVIOUS street (flop checked through to us on the turn, or
// flop+turn checked through on the river). A line that was passive then suddenly
// bets is capped - a delayed stab, not a planned value line. [EM read-the-line]
WHEN IsTurn AND NoVillainBetOrRaisedOnFlop RETURN true FORCE
WHEN IsRiver AND NoVillainBetOrRaisedOnFlop AND NoVillainBetOrRaisedOnTurn RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$OppLineRaisedThisStreet##
// The opponent RAISED us on this street (a check-raise or a raise of our bet).
WHEN Raises >= 1 AND AmountToCall > 0 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$OppRepresents##
// The opponent's betting-line story (0-3). Built bottom-up so the STRONGEST
// credible signals win first.
//
// 3 = STRONG / CREDIBLE (respect, fold marginal, never bluff-raise):
WHEN f$OppLineRaisedThisStreet AND (IsTurn OR IsRiver) RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN Raises >= 2 RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$OppLineRaisedThisStreet AND (f$Opp_IsNit OR f$Opp_IsPassive) RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall > 0 AND (f$Opp_IsNit OR f$Opp_IsPassive) AND NOT f$OppMinLead RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$Opp_PotCommitted AND (f$ScaryBoard OR f$BoardWet) AND AmountToCall > 0 RETURN 3 FORCE
// 1 = CAPPED / WEAK (attack - widen bluff-raises / floats / thin value):
WHEN f$OppMinLead RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall > 0 AND f$OppCheckedPriorStreet RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall > 0 AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish) AND NOT (IsTurn OR IsRiver) RETURN 1 FORCE
// 0 = NO STORY (checked to me / nobody has done anything aggressive):
WHEN f$OppCheckedToMe RETURN 0 FORCE
// 2 = MERGED / STANDARD (a single, ordinary bet) - the default when facing a bet.
WHEN Others RETURN 2 FORCE

##f$OppStoryStrong##
// Convenience gate: RESPECT the line (fold marginal hands, do not bluff-raise).
WHEN f$OppRepresents >= 3 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$OppStoryCapped##
// Convenience gate: ATTACK the line (widen bluff-raise / float / thin value).
// Never "attack" a station/fish by bluffing them OFF a hand - the capped-attack
// downstream is float / thin-VALUE there, never a bluff-raise. [CtM p176 don't
// bluff the fish]
WHEN f$OppRepresents = 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  (3)  RANGE CHART vs OUR HAND  -  "is anything in their range ahead of us?"
//
//  Emrald's rule: "if a hand is not in the range that would beat us, we are SAFE
//  to proceed - bet, call, or check." OpenPPL cannot enumerate equity vs a custom
//  combo range (prwin uses fixed assumptions), so this is a practical MADE-HAND
//  vs REPRESENTED-VALUE-RANGE read: the opponent's line (f$OppRepresents) + the
//  board texture imply the TOP of their value range; we then ask whether OUR made
//  hand class sits above it. The literal 169-combo chart is visualised per-seat in
//  the React table view (the range grid under the HUD). [EM read-the-line][CtM
//  p132 perceived ranges; p202 fold the overpair to the nit; p216-217 raises=nuts]
//=============================================================================

##f$BeatenByOppRange##
// TRUE when the opponent's represented (narrowed) value range contains hands that
// BEAT our current made hand.
// We hold the top of essentially any micro value range -> nothing beats us:
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade RETURN false FORCE
WHEN HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair OR HaveStraight OR HaveFlush OR HaveFullHouse OR HaveQuads OR HaveStraightFlush RETURN false FORCE
// A capped / weak / no story can't credibly hold a hand that beats a real made hand:
WHEN f$OppRepresents <= 1 RETURN false FORCE
// A credible, nut-weighted line (turn/river raise, nit/passive firing, 3-bet line,
// committed on a scary board) beats our one-pair-class holdings:
WHEN f$OppStoryStrong RETURN true FORCE
// One pair facing a standard merged bet on a wet/scary board: hands beat us:
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$OppRepresents >= 2 AND (f$ScaryBoard OR f$BoardWet) RETURN true FORCE
// Otherwise (we hold a decent hand vs a merged range on a dry board) -> ahead:
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$SafeVsOppRange##
// [Emrald] TRUE = NOTHING in the opponent's represented range beats us -> SAFE to
// PROCEED confidently (value-bet, call, or check for value/showdown). FALSE = their
// range has us beat -> pot-control or fold the marginal stuff. This is the positive
// face of f$BeatenByOppRange, used to GREEN-LIGHT thin value + bluff-catches.
WHEN NOT f$BeatenByOppRange RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//=============================================================================
//  (4)  FEELER / INFORMATION BETS + cheap bluff-catch  [Emrald]
//  When I don't yet know where I stand, bet SMALL to (a) gather information - the
//  villain's RESPONSE to the size feeds f$OppRepresents on the next street - and
//  (b) control the pot. Size as LARGE as possible while STILL controlling it. On
//  defence: a small bet into me is cheap to call with any showdown value, and a
//  tiny (~1bb) bet is itself information (a capped/weak line, read by f$OppMinLead).
//=============================================================================

##f$SmallBet##
// The bet facing us is cheap: <= ~1/3 pot (>= 3:1; need <= ~25% equity). Micro
// small/min bets are weak and under-bluff-to-fold. [CtM p210-211][PMM pot odds]
WHEN AmountToCall > 0 AND AmountToCall * 3 <= PotSize RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$WorthCallingSmall##
// Even if I might be behind, a small bet is worth CALLING with any showdown value /
// draw (cheap price vs a capped small bet) - unless the line is a credible nut story.
// [Emrald "if the bet is small it may be worth calling"]
WHEN f$SmallBet AND NOT f$OppStoryStrong AND (f$HaveOnePair OR HaveTopPair OR HaveOverPair OR HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair OR f$HaveBigDraw) RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$WhereAmIUnsure##
// I hold a MARGINAL made hand (one-pair class) and I am neither clearly strong nor told to
// respect a credible line -> the FEELER spot: a small controlled bet learns where I stand and
// keeps the pot manageable, instead of checking blind or over-committing. This is decoupled
// from whether they have bet yet: first-to-act it is a probe; the response is read next street
// by f$OppRepresents. [Emrald feeler system][CtM pot control / sizing-for-info]
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade OR HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair OR HaveStraight OR HaveFlush RETURN false FORCE
WHEN f$OppStoryStrong RETURN false FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair OR HaveTopPair OR HaveOverPair RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$FeelerSize##
// Information / pot-control bet %, "as LARGE as possible while still controlling the
// pot": half-pot default (gets a read AND charges draws); ~1/3 on dry boards vs
// stations (cheaper, they tell you anyway); ~1/4 multiway or very deep (pure
// information, minimise risk). The villain's RESPONSE to this size is then read by
// f$OppRepresents on the next street. [Emrald feeler system][CtM p150 sizing-for-info]
WHEN nopponentsplaying > 2 RETURN 25 FORCE
WHEN f$BoardParched AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish) RETURN 33 FORCE
WHEN f$EffStack > 150 RETURN 33 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 50 FORCE

##f$FeelerBet##
// Fire a feeler when I'm unsure where I am AND I can take a controlled stab with the
// lead / position (NOT out of position into the aggressor - that's the check-call
// rhythm of f$ActBeforeAggressor). [Emrald]
WHEN f$WhereAmIUnsure AND NOT f$ActBeforeAggressor AND (f$InPositionPost OR f$IAmAggressor) RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  13_streetplan - the STREET-STRATEGY FORMER (multi-street planning).
//
//  Forms ONE line that applies across streets instead of deciding each street in
//  isolation -- "flat the flop, then represent the flush & barrel a scare card",
//  "check-raise then keep barreling", "value three streets", "pot-control". It
//  considers BUCKETS of the villain's exploit pathways (via the f$Exploit_* reads)
//  and is driven by the harmonized INTUITION (11_introspection). The intuition
//  inputs are stable across streets, so the plan holds. Codes match brain_state:
//    1 pot_control  2 value_three_streets  3 flat_then_bluff_scare
//    4 check_raise_barrel  5 delayed_cbet  6 give_up  7 show_of_force  0 none
//  The richer plan former is the live advisor (decision_advisor.py); this is the
//  always-on OHF fallback the deep-rewire (50/60/70) executes toward.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$Plan##
WHEN f$Intuition_ShowOfForce RETURN 7 FORCE
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade AND NOT f$Exploit_KeepsFiring RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND FlushPossible RETURN 3 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp OR f$Exploit_FastWeak RETURN 4 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_Tilt RETURN 2 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_KeepsFiring RETURN 1 FORCE
WHEN f$Exploit_NeverFolds AND NOT f$HaveStrongMade RETURN 6 FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN 0 FORCE

##f$Plan_IsShowOfForce##
WHEN f$Plan = 7 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Plan_IsValueTriple##
WHEN f$Plan = 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Plan_IsBluffScare##
// flat / cheap now, then represent the flush (or a scare card) and barrel on a later street
WHEN f$Plan = 3 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Plan_IsCheckRaiseBarrel##
WHEN f$Plan = 4 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Plan_IsPotControl##
WHEN f$Plan = 1 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$Plan_IsGiveUp##
WHEN f$Plan = 6 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

// The ismyturn loop asks: is THIS street's pathway already in the plan + considered?
##f$Plan_PathwayConsidered##
WHEN f$Plan = 0 RETURN false FORCE
WHEN f$Plan_IsBluffScare AND (IsTurn OR IsRiver) AND FlushPossible RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Plan_IsValueTriple RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Plan_IsCheckRaiseBarrel RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Plan_IsShowOfForce RETURN true FORCE
WHEN f$Plan_IsPotControl AND AmountToCall > 0 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  15_explain - human-readable, variable-filled decision explanations (VERBOSE).
//
//  Each f$expl_<tag> holds its explanation TEMPLATE on a "//~" comment line
//  (the parser ignores comments, so any {placeholders}, %, $ etc. are safe).
//  The function body is a trivial "0" that is never used: the explain engine
//  reads the template from the "//~" comment, substitutes {tokens} with live
//  values, and prints the result to the Decisions pane when the matching
//  explain_<tag> symbol is reached at the TAIL of a WHEN condition, e.g.
//
//      WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysStrong AND explain_fold_tank Fold FORCE
//
//  {tokens} may be any symbol or f$function. Emission is de-duplicated and is
//  suppressed during parsing. Verbose = full spot (stack/pot/opp/equity) + the
//  REASONING in plain English, so the Decisions pane reads like a coach talking.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$expl_open##
//~ OPEN-RAISE to {f$Open_RaiseTo}bb. First in from my {f$Style}-style positional range, {nopponentsplaying} left to act, effective {f$EffStack}bb, ~{tgi_players_remaining} players left. Taking the initiative and the dead money rather than limping; if 3-bet I have a plan. [conf {validator_confidence}]
0

##f$expl_iso##
//~ ISO-RAISE to {f$Iso_RaiseTo}bb over {Calls} limper(s). Punishing the limp - they entered weak/passive, so I size up to play a bigger pot in position with the better hand and deny them a cheap flop. Eff {f$EffStack}bb, pot building to {PotSize}bb.
0

##f$expl_3bet_value##
//~ 3-BET to {f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo}bb FOR VALUE. Premium vs a single open (opener VPIP {f$Opp_VPIP}, PFR {f$Opp_PFR}, AF {f$Opp_AF}). I want money in now while ahead of his opening range; building a pot I expect to win. Eff {f$EffStack}bb.
0

##f$expl_3bet_bluff##
//~ 3-BET BLUFF to {f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo}bb, in position vs a foldy/loose opener (VPIP {f$Opp_VPIP}, PFR {f$Opp_PFR}). Ace-blocker / playable suited, mixed frequency. He opens too wide and folds too much to pressure, so I attack; if called I have equity and position. Eff {f$EffStack}bb.
0

##f$expl_call_setmine##
//~ CALL to SET-MINE. Risking {AmountToCall}bb of my {f$EffStack}bb with a small/medium pair for the implied odds (enough stack behind to get paid - ~15x+ vs an open, or <=~10% of stack vs a 3-bet) - I am hunting a flopped set to stack him; folding everything else. Pot {PotSize}bb, ~{tgi_players_remaining} left.
0

##f$expl_flat_ip##
//~ FLAT IN POSITION. Calling {AmountToCall}bb with a hand that plays well postflop (suited broadway / connector / pair) rather than 3-betting - keeping his range wide and his bluffs in, then outplaying him after the flop with position. Pot {PotSize}bb, eff {f$EffStack}bb.
0

##f$expl_bbdefend##
//~ DEFEND BIG BLIND. Getting a price ({AmountToCall}bb into {PotSize}bb) closing the action, so I call wide to realize equity rather than fold my big-blind investment. Will play fit-or-fold flops in a bloated-enough pot. Eff {f$EffStack}bb.
0

##f$expl_pushfold##
//~ PUSH/FOLD MODE. Effective {f$EffStack}bb (<=~15, or M<=5) - too short to play postflop, so it is shove-or-fold. Jamming a position-scaled near-Nash range to maximize fold equity + pick up {PotSize}bb of blinds/antes. Survival = chips; a timely jam beats blinding out. ~{tgi_players_remaining} left.
0

##f$expl_jam##
//~ ALL-IN JAM for {f$EffStack}bb. Short-stack first-in shove from my position range - fold equity is the whole point; folding strong hands here is the leak that blinds you out. Picking up {PotSize}bb dead money now. ~{tgi_players_remaining} left.
0

##f$expl_callshove##
//~ CALL THE SHOVE. Getting it in for {f$EffStack}bb vs a single all-in, far enough from the money that it is chip-EV - my hand crushes his shoving range and I have the equity + price. Not folding a strong holding short. Pot {PotSize}bb.
0

##f$expl_cbet##
//~ C-BET ~{f$BetPctFlop}% pot ({PotSize}bb). I raised pre and keep the lead on a board that misses his range more than mine, vs a foldy/heads-up opp (VPIP {f$Opp_VPIP}, AF {f$Opp_AF}); my equity {prwin}. Denying his free cards and taking it down often right here.
0

##f$expl_value_flop##
//~ VALUE BET ~{f$BetPctFlop}% pot ({PotSize}bb). Strong made hand, equity {prwin} - I size up to charge his draws and worse pairs, building the pot while I am ahead. He pays or folds equity; either is good. vs VPIP {f$Opp_VPIP}.
0

##f$expl_semibluff##
//~ SEMI-BLUFF ~{f$BetPctFlop}% pot ({PotSize}bb). Big/combo draw - two ways to win: he folds now, or I hit. Equity {prwin}. Betting (not checking) so I can win it without showdown AND get paid when I improve. Eff {f$EffStack}bb.
0

##f$expl_fold_tank##
//~ FOLD one pair. The raiser TANKED {lastraiseractiontime}s (>= {f$TankSeconds}s) before betting - a long think here screams strength/value, not a bluff. One pair is not worth {AmountToCall}bb into {PotSize}bb against that. Disciplined laydown; don't go broke with one pair.
0

##f$expl_float_snap##
//~ FLOAT / CALL one pair. The raiser SNAP-bet in {lastraiseractiontime}s (<= {f$SnapSeconds}s) - an instant bet is often a c-bet or weak stab, not a thinking value bet. Calling {AmountToCall}bb into {PotSize}bb to take it away on a later street; equity {prwin}.
0

##f$expl_potcontrol##
//~ CHECK for POT CONTROL. One pair, decent but not great - keeping the pot small (don't stack off with one pair) and getting to showdown cheaply rather than bloating it. Pot {PotSize}bb, eff {f$EffStack}bb, equity {prwin}.
0

##f$expl_value_river##
//~ RIVER VALUE ~{f$BetPctRiver}% pot ({PotSize}bb). Strong made hand at showdown, equity {prwin} - last chance to get value, so I bet a size a worse hand can still call, vs VPIP {f$Opp_VPIP} / AF {f$Opp_AF}. Thin-but-ahead.
0

##f$expl_bluffcatch##
//~ BLUFF-CATCH. Calling {AmountToCall}bb into {PotSize}bb vs an aggressive/snap bettor (AF {f$Opp_AF}, VPIP {f$Opp_VPIP}). My hand only beats bluffs, but his range here is bluff-heavy enough and the price is right; a fold over-folds to aggression.
0

##f$expl_fold_pre##
//~ FOLD preflop. Hand is below my range for this spot (position / action / {f$EffStack}bb depth) - no cheap entry, facing aggression, or out of position. Folding now saves chips for a better spot; patience early is a weapon. ~{tgi_players_remaining} left.
0

//*****************************************************************************
//  16_steering - runtime steering + OpenAI hijack hooks  (advisor DISABLED by
//  default; these are inert until HKCU\Software\ScarletBeast\OpenAiEnabled=1).
//
//  ANCHORS - named entry points the Terminal console can steer to. Each major
//  decision function is tagged with a "// @anchor: <name> (id N)" comment and the
//  ids are mapped in COpenAiAdvisor::AnchorIdFromName():
//      1 preflop   2 flop   3 turn   4 river
//     11 smallball 12 power 13 hybrid   (these retune f$Style live)
//
//  CONSOLE COMMANDS (type into the Terminal prompt or the browser prompt):
//     /stop                 pause (sets openai_paused = 1)
//     /play                 resume
//     /strategy smallball|power|hybrid   retune the profile live (via f$Style)
//     /goto <anchor>        set openai_steer_anchor
//     /hijack [why]         send state+context+chat+decisions to OpenAI
//     /improve <text>       propose an .ohf edit (written to Strategy\proposed\)
//
//  SYMBOLS (provided by CSymbolEngineOpenAI):
//     openai_paused        1 while /stop is active
//     openai_steer_anchor  the steered anchor id (0 = none)
//     openai_action        OpenAI's recommended action, or a no-opinion sentinel
//     openai_autohijack    1 if auto-hijack-on-no-fit is enabled
//     openai_consult       TRIGGER (true) -> consults OpenAI on a no-fit spot
//
//  The openai_action override is already wired at the top of f$preflop / f$flop /
//  f$turn / f$river: when the advisor returns a concrete raise size it is taken,
//  otherwise (the default, disabled) the sentinel keeps the bot on its own logic.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$Paused##
// Convenience mirror of the /stop state for use in your own gating if desired.
WHEN openai_paused RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$NoHeuristicFit##
// Mark a spot the hand-coded strategy does not cover well. Edit this to taste;
// when true (and auto-hijack is enabled) f$ConsultOpenAI will ask for help.
// Example heuristics for "weird, low-confidence" spots:
WHEN BotsActionsOnThisRound > 2 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ConsultOpenAI##
// Call this where you want an auto-consult on no-fit spots, e.g. add
//   WHEN f$NoHeuristicFit AND f$ConsultOpenAI Check FORCE
// near a fallback. openai_consult fires the (disabled-by-default) advisor and
// returns true; we then Check as a safe default. Inert while the advisor is off.
WHEN openai_consult RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  20_lists - hand ranges (synthesis of [N] and [B]).
//  Shared ground: both love SUITED CONNECTORS and SMALL PAIRS (flop a monster,
//  win a big pot) [N pp.15-16][B p.487]; Brunson adds "ace/king + any suited =
//  two shots" [B p.508]; Negreanu adds wide late-position steals [N listOpenBTN].
//*****************************************************************************

##listPremium##
// Get-it-in-pre tier.
AA  KK  QQ  AKs  AKo

##listBigPair##
AA  KK  QQ  JJ

##listSetMine##
// Small/medium pairs we flat to flop a set (never reraise pre). [N p.21][B p.481]
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT

##listSmallSuitedConnectors##
// Small suited connectors -- cheap, high-implied-value hands that flop big draws/two-pair+ multiway.
// Limp these in behind limpers whenever the depth gives implied odds. [Emrald: limp small SCs when you can]
98s 87s 76s 65s 54s 43s 32s

##listAceRag##
// Weak (offsuit) aces -- "ace rag". Limp them in cheaply; if we catch an ace we play passive pot-control
// (don't raise top pair / weak kicker), call little bets, get to a cheap showdown. [Emrald: limp ace rag]
A9o A8o A7o A6o A5o A4o A3o A2o

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Open-raise ranges (first in), widening by position.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##listOpenEP##
// Early position (~16%): pairs, suited broadways, the better suited connectors.
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
ATs AJs AQs AKs KTs KJs KQs QTs QJs JTs T9s 98s 87s 76s
AJo AQo AKo KQo

##listOpenMP##
// Middle position (~22%): add suited aces, more suited gappers/connectors.
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
K9s KTs KJs KQs Q9s QTs QJs J9s JTs T8s T9s 97s 98s 87s 76s 65s 54s
ATo AJo AQo AKo KJo KQo

##listOpenLP##
// Cutoff / late (~32%): all suited aces, suited kings, more connectors & gappers.
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
K5s K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs Q8s Q9s QTs QJs J8s J9s JTs T7s T8s T9s 96s 97s 98s 86s 87s 75s 76s 65s 54s 43s
A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo K9o KTo KJo KQo Q9o QTo QJo J9o JTo T9o

##listOpenBTN##
// Button (~48%, very wide). Position + "any two" pressure. [N][B p.509]
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
K2s K3s K4s K5s K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs
Q4s Q5s Q6s Q7s Q8s Q9s QTs QJs J6s J7s J8s J9s JTs T6s T7s T8s T9s 95s 96s 97s 98s 85s 86s 87s 74s 75s 76s 64s 65s 53s 54s 43s
A2o A3o A4o A5o A6o A7o A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo K7o K8o K9o KTo KJo KQo Q8o Q9o QTo QJo J8o J9o JTo T8o T9o 98o 87o

##listOpenSB##
// Small blind, folded to us: late-position width but a touch more cautious OOP.
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs Q8s Q9s QTs QJs J8s J9s JTs T7s T8s T9s 96s 97s 98s 86s 87s 75s 76s 65s 54s
A7o A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo K9o KTo KJo KQo Q9o QTo QJo J9o JTo T9o

##listStealNit##
// EXPLOIT range (~65%): used ONLY to open-steal into confirmed nitty blinds (f$BlindsAreNitty) from a
// steal position. Nits over-fold the blinds, so we widen toward any-two: all pairs, ALL suited, every
// offsuit ace/king, most offsuit broadways, and the offsuit connectors. [N "attack the weak-tight"]
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
K2s K3s K4s K5s K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs
Q2s Q3s Q4s Q5s Q6s Q7s Q8s Q9s QTs QJs
J2s J3s J4s J5s J6s J7s J8s J9s JTs
T2s T3s T4s T5s T6s T7s T8s T9s
92s 93s 94s 95s 96s 97s 98s 82s 83s 84s 85s 86s 87s 72s 73s 74s 75s 76s 62s 63s 64s 65s 52s 53s 54s 42s 43s 32s
A2o A3o A4o A5o A6o A7o A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo
K2o K3o K4o K5o K6o K7o K8o K9o KTo KJo KQo
Q5o Q6o Q7o Q8o Q9o QTo QJo J7o J8o J9o JTo T7o T8o T9o 98o 87o 76o 65o 54o

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Push/fold JAM ranges (effective stack <= ~15bb, the f$PushFoldStack ceiling).
//  Near-Nash, position-scaled.
//  At these depths strong broadways (KJ/QJ/KT/QT/JT) and any ace/pair are SHOVES,
//  not folds - folding them is the leak that blinds a short stack out. [Nash push]
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##listJamLP##
// Button / cutoff / late / SB first-in: very wide (~55-60%).
22 33 44 55 66 77 88 99 TT JJ QQ KK AA
A2s A3s A4s A5s A6s A7s A8s A9s ATs AJs AQs AKs
K2s K3s K4s K5s K6s K7s K8s K9s KTs KJs KQs
Q2s Q3s Q4s Q5s Q6s Q7s Q8s Q9s QTs QJs
J5s J6s J7s J8s J9s JTs T6s T7s T8s T9s 95s 96s 97s 98s 85s 86s 87s 75s 76s 64s 65s 54s 43s
A2o A3o A4o A5o A6o A7o A8o A9o ATo AJo AQo AKo
K5o K6o K7o K8o K9o KTo KJo KQo Q7o Q8o Q9o QTo QJo J7o J8o J9o JTo T7o T8o T9o 97o 98o 87o

