//*****************************************************************************
//  30_classify - made-hand / draw / board-texture classification.
//  Wraps the built-in Have* and board symbols into the concepts the two
//  strategies reason about.
//*****************************************************************************

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Made-hand tiers
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$HaveBigMade##
// Straight or better - the hands you commit with. [N "near-nuts"][B set+]
WHEN HaveStraight OR HaveFlush OR HaveFullHouse OR HaveQuads RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveStrongMade##
// Two pair / set / big made, or a clean overpair-top-pair on a dry board.
WHEN HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair OR f$HaveBigMade RETURN true FORCE
WHEN (HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair) AND NOT FlushPossible AND NOT StraightPossible RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveOnePair##
// The classic trap class: one pair, however big. "Don't go broke with one pair." [N p.125]
WHEN HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveDecentMade##
WHEN HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair OR HaveTwoPair OR HaveSet OR f$HaveBigMade RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveMarginalMade##
// Weak pair / second pair / bottom pair - showdown value, not betting value.
WHEN f$HaveDecentMade RETURN false FORCE
WHEN HavePair OR HaveBottomPair RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Draws
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$HaveBigDraw##
// The draws Brunson plays FAST (semi-bluff / shove). [B D6.1-D6.2]
WHEN HaveNutFlushDraw OR HaveFlushDraw OR HaveOpenEndedStraightDraw RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveComboDraw##
// Pair+draw or two draws - "two ways to win", get it in. [B D6.6]
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND (HavePair OR HaveInsideStraightDraw) RETURN true FORCE
WHEN HaveFlushDraw AND HaveOpenEndedStraightDraw RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveWeakDraw##
WHEN HaveInsideStraightDraw OR HaveBackdoorFlushDraw RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$HaveAnyDraw##
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveWeakDraw RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Board texture
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$BoardWet##
// Draw-heavy / coordinated: charge draws, slow down marginal hands.
WHEN FlushPossible OR StraightPossible OR FlushDrawPossible RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$BoardDry##
// Hit-or-miss board: your pair is likely still good; cheap to give a free card. [N p.63]
WHEN NOT FlushPossible AND NOT StraightPossible AND NOT FlushDrawPossible RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$ScaryBoard##
// Brunson "frightening flop": someone surely connected - don't bluff into it. [B R5.3]
WHEN FlushPossible OR StraightOnBoard OR MoreThanOneStraightPossibleOnFlop RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  HIGH-CARD board texture for c-bet bluffs (Gordon's combinatoric read). The
//  existing wet/dry/scary symbols are DRAW-based and blind to the board's HIGH
//  card. A flat-caller's range is loaded with broadways: a K/A/Q-high DRY flop
//  MISSES that range (few of those cards remain) -> great bluff-c-bet card; a
//  J/T-high DRY flop HITS it hard -> do NOT bluff-c-bet. [GG "Continuation-Bets
//  for Bluffs", "Low/Paired/Monotone Boards", "Parched Boards"]
//  HighestRankOnFlop is the numeric top board rank (Queen=12, King=13, Ace=14).
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$BoardHighCardFoldy##
// Dry board whose HIGH card is Q+ (>=12): few Q/K/A combos left in a caller's
// flat range, so an air c-bet picks it up. Boost/keep the bluff-c-bet here.
WHEN f$BoardDry AND HighestRankOnFlop >= 12 RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$BoardHighCardSticky##
// Dry board topped by a Jack or Ten (HighestRankOnFlop 10 or 11): HITS a flat
// caller's broadway-heavy range - do NOT fire an air c-bet here. (Q+ excluded.)
// Defined as the dry-board residue of the other two textures: a dry flop is exactly
// one of Foldy (Q+), Parched (<=9, no ace), or Sticky (J/T-high) - so this wires
// f$BoardHighCardFoldy + f$BoardParched into the live c-bet path (50_flop) instead of
// duplicating the rank thresholds. Behaviour-identical to "HighestRankOnFlop 10-11".
WHEN f$BoardDry AND NOT f$BoardHighCardFoldy AND NOT f$BoardParched RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$BoardParched##
// Low, rainbow, disconnected "parched" flop (e.g. 7-4-2 / 9-6-3 / 8-5-4): top card
// 9 or below AND dry. Misses everyone - barrel the whole range relentlessly; only
// slow/fold when an Ace turns (handled on the turn via AcePresentOnTurn). [GG]
WHEN f$BoardDry AND HighestRankOnFlop <= 9 AND NOT AcePresentOnFlop RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Initiative
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$WasPreflopRaiser##
WHEN BotRaisedBeforeFlop RETURN true FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  40_preflop - the pre-flop decision tree.
//
//  Dispatch by the number of raises this round:
//    Raises == 0  -> unopened or limped pot  (open / iso-raise / over-limp)
//    Raises == 1  -> facing a single open    (3-bet value/bluff / flat / fold)
//    Raises >= 2  -> facing a 3-bet+          (4-bet value / call IP / fold)
//  Very short stacks switch to a push/fold game. [N p.34][B S8.3]
//*****************************************************************************

##f$preflop##
// SLOW-PLAY MEMORY RESET (Emrald): clear the per-hand slow-play flag at the start of each hand (memory
// persists across hands in this build). me_st_slowplay_0 stores 0 and returns 0, so "0 < 0" is ALWAYS
// false -> this never fires / never changes the action; it only resets the flag. [slow-play memory symbol]
WHEN me_st_slowplay_0 < 0 RETURN Fold FORCE
// ACE-RAG MEMORY RESET (Emrald): same trick -- clear the per-hand ace-rag passive-line flag each hand (stores
// 0, returns 0, "0 < 0" is always false -> never fires, only resets). [Emrald: ace-rag memory symbol]
WHEN me_st_acerag_0 < 0 RETURN Fold FORCE
// SCRAPE SAFETY GATE: if the validator flags a HARD scrape error (impossible cards,
// chips that don't conserve, a bad/negative pot), do NOT commit chips on garbage data.
// Check when it's free, otherwise fold. Complements the C++ CSymbolEngineValidator.
// Scrape safety gate: on a hard-flagged mis-scrape, CHECK if it's free. We deliberately
// do NOT auto-fold here -- folding a made hand on a transient bad frame is worse than the
// mis-scrape (it folded a made straight once). Facing a bet, fall through to normal logic.
WHEN validator_ok = 0 AND AmountToCall = 0 Check FORCE
// POT-COMMITTED DUST: once we've put >= 2bb in this round and our remaining stack can no longer
// cover the call (so calling is itself all-in), NEVER fold the committed chips -- jam the sliver.
// The pot odds on our last chips are astronomical; folding them is pure loss. This is the
// 14bb-shove-then-fold-0.21bb leak on hand 2763842893. Placed above every dispatch (incl. the
// push/fold fold lines) so it pre-empts them. Uses only stock symbols (no rebuild). [Emrald]
WHEN currentbet >= 2 * bblind AND balance <= AmountToCall AND balance > 0 RaiseMax FORCE
// BRAIN-ACTION soft pre-empt (Phase 2): the synapse current_decided_action, conf-gated. DISABLED by
// default (the Python only pushes brain_action when enabled, so brain_action_kind is stale=0 and this
// never fires); when enabled it lets a CONFIDENT brain decision drive the commit. [Emrald]
WHEN brain_action_kind >= 1 AND brain_action_conf >= 0.60 RETURN f$BrainAction FORCE
// @anchor: preflop (id 1)
// OpenAI hijack override: when the advisor is enabled and returns a concrete
// raise size, take it. Disabled -> openai_action is the kOpenAiNoOpinion sentinel
// (<= -1000), so this never fires and play is unchanged. [steering]
WHEN openai_action > -1000 RETURN openai_action FORCE
// OBSERVER GOTO (Phase 2): the observer branch's forced line, never over push/fold ICM. f$ObsStrategy is
// -1 today (the branch steers via the obsbranch_* knobs in f$AggroFreqMult/etc.), so this is an inert,
// wired hook; per-branch FORCED lines drop into f$ObsStrategy in 11_introspection later. [Emrald]
WHEN f$ObsStrategy >= 0 AND f$PushFoldStack = 0 RETURN f$ObsStrategy FORCE
// GAME-TYPE DISPATCH: route Omaha / Omaha-Hi-Lo to their own trees (Strategy\Omaha\ & \Omaha8\). isplo8
// implies isomaha, so test it first. Falls through to the Hold'em logic below when neither is set. This
// was present in bot_logic/Strategy/40_preflop.ohf but MISSING from the generated master, so the master's
// f$preflop (which wins at load) never dispatched -> PLO/PLO8 ran the Hold'em preflop tree on 2 of 4
// cards and never raised. [Emrald: "I dont see PLO or PLO8 raising at all" -- 2026-06-20]
WHEN isplo8 RETURN f$preflop_plo8 FORCE
WHEN isomaha RETURN f$preflop_omaha FORCE
WHEN f$PushFoldStack RETURN f$preflop_pushfold FORCE
// 16-25bb fold-equity 3-bet-jam over a single open (re-steal band). [JL][RE]
WHEN f$ReshoveSpot AND explain_jam RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN Raises >= 2 RETURN f$preflop_vs_3bet FORCE
WHEN Raises == 1 RETURN f$preflop_vs_raise FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$preflop_open FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Unopened / limped pots
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$preflop_open##
WHEN Calls >= 1 RETURN f$preflop_limped FORCE
// Truly unopened: open-raise by position. Short stacks tighten to the MP range.
WHEN f$ShortStack AND NOT listOpenMP Fold FORCE
// OPENING-RANGE KNOB (tighten): when the Synapse open-range dial is turned DOWN, open only the
// MP-strength range from every seat (drop the wide late/blind steals). BB still checks. Inert at
// the neutral / wide settings. [Emrald open-range knob]
WHEN f$OpenTightenHard AND NOT InBigBlind AND NOT listOpenMP AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
// Heads-up: the button/SB opens very wide at a minraise. [HUM][HUSNG]
WHEN f$HeadsUpPot AND InSmallBlind AND listOpenHU AND explain_open RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo_HU FORCE
// EXPLOIT (observationally learned -- observe_learn flagged nits like H1GHJACK / metared): confirmed
// nitty blinds (f$BlindsAreNitty, via pt_*_smallblind/bigblind) over-fold to opens, so open MUCH wider
// from the steal seats (listStealNit ~65%). Short stacks already folded their junk above, so this only
// widens healthy-stack steals; non-nit blinds fall through to the normal positional opens. [N p.30]
WHEN (InButton OR InCutOff) AND f$BlindsAreNitty AND listStealNit AND explain_open RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InSmallBlind AND f$BlindsAreNitty AND listStealNit AND explain_open RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
// OPENING-RANGE KNOB (widen): when the Synapse open-range dial is turned UP, open the wide ~65%
// steal list from any late seat / the SB regardless of the blinds' tendency. Inert at neutral /
// tight. [Emrald open-range knob]
WHEN f$OpenWiden AND (InButton OR InCutOff OR InLatePosition) AND listStealNit AND explain_open RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN f$OpenWiden AND InSmallBlind AND listStealNit AND explain_open RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
// 6-max: tighter early/middle than the full-ring-shared lists. [RF][V6]
WHEN f$Is6Max AND InEarlyPosition AND listOpenEP6 RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN f$Is6Max AND InMiddlePosition AND listOpenMP6 RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InEarlyPosition AND listOpenEP RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InMiddlePosition AND listOpenMP RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN (InLatePosition OR InCutOff) AND listOpenLP RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InButton AND listOpenBTN AND explain_open RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InSmallBlind AND listOpenSB RaiseTo f$Open_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InBigBlind Check FORCE
WHEN explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE

##f$preflop_limped##
// Limpers (1bb bettors) in front: PUNISH the limp with a ~5bb iso-raise (f$Iso_RaiseTo,
// +1bb per extra limper) using the positional OPEN ranges -- this RAISES KJ/broadway-type
// hands (e.g. KdJd) instead of flatting them. Speculative hands set-mine cheaply; trash
// folds. [N p.24][B]
// OVER-LIMP (Emrald): occasionally just LIMP behind the limpers instead of always iso-raising -- balances
// our limped range and buys a cheap multiway flop to stack them when we connect. Speculative set-mine hands
// at LOW frequency (~9%) so we still mostly punish. [Emrald: sometimes limp in with the limpers, not often]
WHEN listSetMine AND randomround < 0.09 Call FORCE
// Small suited connectors: limp them in behind the limpers WHENEVER the depth gives implied odds (they flop
// big draws / two-pair+ multiway and are cheap to see a flop with). [Emrald: limp small SCs when you can]
WHEN listSmallSuitedConnectors AND f$SetMineOK Call FORCE
// ACE-RAG: limp weak aces in cheaply (when the depth gives implied odds) instead of iso-raising, and SET the
// ace-rag memory flag so the flop knows to play the passive pot-control line. [Emrald: limp ace rag when you can]
WHEN listAceRag AND f$SetMineOK AND me_st_acerag_1 Call FORCE
WHEN (listBigPair OR list3betValue) AND explain_iso RaiseTo f$Iso_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InEarlyPosition AND listOpenEP AND explain_iso RaiseTo f$Iso_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InMiddlePosition AND listOpenMP AND explain_iso RaiseTo f$Iso_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN (InLatePosition OR InCutOff OR InButton) AND listOpenLP AND explain_iso RaiseTo f$Iso_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN InSmallBlind AND listOpenMP AND explain_iso RaiseTo f$Iso_RaiseTo FORCE
WHEN f$DeepStack AND listSetMine Call FORCE
WHEN InBigBlind Check FORCE
WHEN explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Facing a single open raise
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$preflop_vs_raise##
// Vs a player who 3-bets light, just FLAT the premiums and outplay him. [N p.22]
WHEN list3betValue AND f$Opp_ThreeBetsLight AND listCall3bet Call FORCE
// CtM: vs a NIT'S open, FLAT the big pairs / big aces (in position or at a price)
// instead of 3-betting. A nit's opening range is so tight it crushes JJ/AK, so bloating
// the pot only folds out everything we beat and gets it in behind. Flat and set-mine /
// outplay rather than 3-bet into his nut-weighted range. [CtM p96 "vs a nit opening EP,
// calling is often best with big aces/pairs"; p106 "a nit opens EP -> flat call"]
WHEN list3betValue AND f$Opp_IsNit AND (f$InPositionPre OR f$DecentPrice) AND listCall3bet Call FORCE
// 3-bet for value.
WHEN list3betValue AND explain_3bet_value RaiseTo f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo FORCE
// SQUEEZE: a raise WITH cold-caller(s) in front -> 3-bet to isolate with a value range.
// Flatting OOP in the blinds doesn't even close the action (BB acts behind the SB), so a
// strong broadway like AJo must squeeze rather than fold/flat multiway. [N p.26]
WHEN Calls >= 1 AND listSqueeze AND explain_3bet_value RaiseTo f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo FORCE
// 3-bet bluff in position at an opponent-typed frequency (f$ThreeBetBluffFreq returns 0
// vs stations/light-3bettors, high vs nits/foldy). [ER p7][LTBR p11][N p.26]
WHEN list3betBluff AND f$InPositionPre AND randomround < f$ThreeBetBluffFreq RaiseTo f$ThreeBet_RaiseTo FORCE
// Heads-up big-blind defence: flat WIDE vs a single SB open (don't over-fold). [HUSNG p27]
WHEN InBigBlind AND f$HeadsUpPot AND listDefendHU AND explain_bbdefend Call FORCE
// Flat to set-mine / play suited hands, in position or getting a price.
WHEN listCallOpen AND f$InPositionPre AND explain_flat_ip Call FORCE
WHEN listSetMine AND f$DeepStack AND f$SetMineOK AND explain_call_setmine Call FORCE
// Big-blind defence: defend a price with playable hands.
WHEN InBigBlind AND listCallOpen AND explain_bbdefend Call FORCE
WHEN InBigBlind AND f$DecentPrice AND listOpenLP Call FORCE
WHEN explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Facing a 3-bet or more (we usually opened)
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$preflop_vs_3bet##
// 4-bet for value.
WHEN list4betValue RaiseTo f$FourBet_RaiseTo FORCE
// Power-poker: also 4-bet QQ/AK for value vs a 3-bet. [B]
WHEN f$Style == 1 AND list4betValuePower RaiseTo f$FourBet_RaiseTo FORCE
// CtM: at full-ring micros, a 3-bet from a NIT or a PASSIVE player is nut-weighted -
// fold even QQ/JJ/AK a lot (they don't 3-bet light). We have already 4-bet AA/KK above,
// so this folds the next tier down rather than flatting it into a crushing range. The
// general-opponent IP flat below is preserved for the wider/unknown 3-bettors. [CtM p107
// "you should be folding a lot when 3bet, esp OOP"; p109 "fold QQ/JJ/AK to a 4bet/nit"]
WHEN NOT list4betValue AND (f$Opp_IsNit OR f$Opp_IsPassive) AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
// Flat the 3-bet in position (or cheaply) and outplay post-flop. [N p.28]
WHEN listCall3bet AND f$InPositionPre Call FORCE
WHEN listCall3bet AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// Deep speculative set-mine vs a 3-bet only when it risks <= ~10% of stack. [N p.29-30]
WHEN listSetMine AND f$DeepStack AND f$WithinSpecRisk AND explain_call_setmine Call FORCE
WHEN explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Push / fold (effective stack <= ~15bb, or M<=5) - see f$PushFoldStack
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$preflop_pushfold##
// Facing a 3-bet+ (multiway / lots in): tighten to the get-it-in tier.
WHEN Raises >= 2 AND (listBigPair OR list3betValue) AND explain_jam RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN Raises >= 2 AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
// Facing a SINGLE raise/shove: get it in by ICM. Premiums never fold; otherwise call/
// re-jam when the ICM model says getting it in is $-correct (f$ICM_CallShove), with the
// wide chip-EV list as a floor so we still jam the standard get-it-in tier when ICM is
// borderline. Re-jam over a non-allin raise; calls an allin. [ICM + N p.34]
WHEN Raises == 1 AND list3betValue AND explain_callshove RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN Raises == 1 AND f$ICM_CallShove AND explain_callshove RaiseMax FORCE
// ON THE BUBBLE (f$Stage = 2): survival has $-value, so the call-shove boundary tightens to
// the ~top-10% listCallShoveBubble and the wide chip-EV floor is SUPPRESSED (it must not
// re-widen past the ICM-tightened gate above). Inert until a real payout curve is scraped
// (f$NearBubble -> f$Stage 2 stays false today), exactly like f$BubbleTighten. [SoS p61][SNG]
WHEN Raises == 1 AND f$Stage = 2 AND listCallShoveBubble AND explain_callshove RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN Raises == 1 AND f$Stage = 2 AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
WHEN Raises == 1 AND listCallShove AND explain_callshove RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN Raises == 1 AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
// First in: jam a near-Nash, position-scaled range (very wide late). Folding strong
// broadways at <=15bb is the leak that blinds you out.
WHEN (InButton OR InCutOff OR InLatePosition OR InSmallBlind) AND listJamLP AND explain_pushfold RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN InMiddlePosition AND listJamMP AND explain_jam RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN InEarlyPosition AND listJamEP AND explain_jam RaiseMax FORCE
WHEN InBigBlind Check FORCE
WHEN explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  50_flop - flop play.  "The flop is practically the whole game." [B R5.1]
//  Dispatch by whether there is a bet to us.
//*****************************************************************************

##f$flop##
// @anchor: flop (id 2)
// Scrape safety gate: CHECK if free on a hard-flagged mis-scrape; do NOT auto-fold
// (folding a made hand on a transient bad frame is worse). Facing a bet, fall through.
WHEN validator_ok = 0 AND AmountToCall = 0 Check FORCE
WHEN openai_action > -1000 RETURN openai_action FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall == 0 RETURN f$flop_nobet FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$flop_vs_bet FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  No bet to us: value-bet / c-bet / semi-bluff, else check.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$flop_nobet##
// Value & protection with strong made hands (bigger on wet boards - see f$BetPctFlop).
// EXTRACTION is the heart of crushing the micros: "flop a set, hit the pot button" -
// NEVER win a small pot with a big hand; fastplay (no slowplay below quads). Size UP for
// value (pot / even overbet) vs ANY of the passive calling types - station, fish AND SLP -
// they pay on their own hand strength and read a big bet as a bluff. Never attack their
// strength by bluffing; make the money by value-betting BIG. [CtM p193 "extraction - the
// heart of it all"; p147,149 value big vs stations; p169 barrel SLPs/fish; p211 "fish view
// big bets as a bluff"][SunTzu IV "first make yourself invincible"][48L L15 "crush the weak"]
// SLOW-PLAY (Emrald): sometimes TRAP a monster instead of fastplaying it. ~22% of the time, in position +
// heads-up + checked to us, holding a BIG made hand (straight/flush/boat/quads) vs a NON-passive opp
// (stations/fish pay anyway -> keep value-betting them), CHECK to induce a bluff and SET the slow-play
// memory flag (me_st_slowplay_1 stores 1 + returns 1, only when every prior condition holds) so the later
// streets keep the trap on. [Emrald: slow-play nut/strong hands via a memory symbol]
WHEN (f$HaveBigMade OR HaveSet) AND f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND NOT f$Opp_IsStation AND NOT f$Opp_IsFish AND randomhand < 0.30 AND me_st_slowplay_1 RETURN Check FORCE
// ACE-RAG PASSIVE (Emrald): we limped a weak ace and CAUGHT one (top pair, weak kicker). Do NOT bet/raise
// it -- pot-control. Only the big-hand lines below (two pair / set / big draw = lots of outs) get to bet.
// [Emrald: catch an ace -> don't raise; only raise w/ lots of outs or two pair]
WHEN me_re_acerag = 1 AND HaveTopPair AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw RETURN Check FORCE
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsSLP) AND explain_value_flop RaiseBy f$BetPctVsStation % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade AND explain_value_flop RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// SUPERSTITION (666 Card Oracle): when the Beast favors, fire EVERY draw as a semibluff.
// sb_beastfavor is 0 unless card_oracle.py --superstition is feeding the omen -> inert when off.
WHEN (f$HaveWeakDraw OR f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveComboDraw) AND sb_beastfavor >= 0.66 RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// Semi-bluff strong & combo draws - two ways to win. [B D6]
WHEN f$HaveComboDraw AND explain_semibluff RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// DRAW MIX (Emrald): a bare big draw (4 to a straight/flush) doesn't ALWAYS want to raise -- ~58% semi-bluff,
// else just take the free card / call at a price below. Keeps us from blasting every draw face-up.
// [Emrald: four to a straight/flush with outs -- not always a raise]
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$Opp_IsStation AND randomround < 0.58 RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// RHYTHM (Emrald 2026-06-20): in position as the flat-caller (NOT the pre-flop raiser), the play is
// usually to CHECK BACK to the raiser - take the free card and see the turn / their next action to
// gather information before committing. Strong made hands (value, above) and big/combo-draw
// semibluffs (above) still fire; this governs the marginal one-pair / air spots in position so we
// act on information, not ahead of it. [info before action; pot control; delayed decision]
WHEN f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND NOT f$WasPreflopRaiser AND NOT f$HaveStrongMade Check FORCE
// RHYTHM (12_aggressor): when an opponent holds the initiative and I act BEFORE him
// (out of position vs the aggressor), do NOT lead a marginal hand into him - CHECK and
// let HIM do the betting, then call with the good-but-not-monster hands. Strong made
// (value, above) and big/combo draws (semibluff, above) still fired; this governs the
// one-pair / weak spots so I act on his information, not ahead of it. [CtM p59 OOP play
// blind; p168 pot-control / check OOP][Tao ch.78 "the soft and yielding overcomes"]
WHEN f$ActBeforeAggressor AND NOT f$HaveStrongMade AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw Check FORCE
// One pair: bet to protect on wet boards or for thin value vs a station; as the
// pre-flop raiser take the small pot now; otherwise pot-control. [N p.125]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$BoardWet RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$Opp_IsStation RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$WasPreflopRaiser RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// Continuation-bet with air as the pre-flop raiser. Skip scary boards & stations;
// bias to heads-up / foldy opponents; frequency set by style. [B R1.3][N ~60%]
WHEN f$WasPreflopRaiser AND f$ScaryBoard Check FORCE
WHEN f$WasPreflopRaiser AND f$Opp_IsStation Check FORCE
// Gordon high-card read: a J/T-high DRY flop HITS a flat-caller's broadway-heavy
// range - don't bluff-c-bet it; check the air. (K/A/Q-high dry "foldy" boards and
// low "parched" boards keep firing below at f$CbetFreq.) [GG bluff-c-bet boards]
WHEN f$WasPreflopRaiser AND f$BoardHighCardSticky Check FORCE
WHEN f$WasPreflopRaiser AND f$HeadsUpPot AND randomround < f$CbetFreq AND explain_cbet RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN f$WasPreflopRaiser AND f$Opp_Foldy AND randomround < f$CbetFreq RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// SHORT-STACK PRESSURE (Emrald): vs a SHORT-STACKED opponent who is likely on air (foldy), apply MORE
// pressure than a normal c-bet -- a short stack can't call light, so a bet folds them right out of the
// hand. Higher frequency, heads-up. [Emrald: pressure little stacks when they likely have nothing]
WHEN f$ShortStack AND f$Opp_Foldy AND f$HeadsUpPot AND randomround < 0.70 RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// In-position stab to set up a turn take-away with a weak draw. [N float doctrine]
WHEN f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND f$HaveWeakDraw AND randomround < 0.50 RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// FEELER (12_aggressor): rather than checking blind with a marginal made hand, fire a SMALL
// controlled bet (f$FeelerSize - as large as possible while still controlling the pot) to gather
// information and keep the pot manageable. Only IP or with the initiative (never OOP into the
// aggressor - that stays a check above). The villain's response feeds f$OppRepresents next street.
// [Emrald feeler/information-bet system]
WHEN f$FeelerBet RaiseBy f$FeelerSize % FORCE
// One pair that did not bet above (not wet / not vs a station / not the PFR): keep the
// pot small and get to showdown cheaply - don't go broke with one pair. [N p.125]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND explain_potcontrol Check FORCE
WHEN Others Check FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Facing a bet on the flop.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$flop_vs_bet##
// Value-raise the big made hands (charge draws; build the pot). [B R5.5]
WHEN f$HaveBigMade RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// ACE-RAG PASSIVE vs a bet (Emrald): top pair / weak kicker -> CALL only a little bet (cheap to improve or
// reach showdown), FOLD to anything bigger. Two pair+/sets already raised above; a big draw (lots of outs)
// falls through to the draw lines. [Emrald: call little bets to improve / get to showdown cheaply]
WHEN me_re_acerag = 1 AND HaveTopPair AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw AND f$SmallBet RETURN Call FORCE
WHEN me_re_acerag = 1 AND HaveTopPair AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw RETURN Fold FORCE
// Low SPR (committed): get top pair / overpair all-in rather than pot-controlling.
// This is the LOW-SPR branch of "don't go broke with one pair" - at high SPR the
// peel/pot-control lines below still apply (NOT f$Committed). [SSNL SPR sidebar]
WHEN (HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair OR f$HaveStrongMade) AND f$Committed RaiseMax FORCE
// Combo draw -> get it all in (two ways to win). [B D6.6]
WHEN f$HaveComboDraw RaiseMax FORCE
// Brunson plays big draws fast even facing a bet; otherwise call at a price.
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND f$Style = 1 RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND f$CheapDraw Call FORCE
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND f$DecentPrice AND f$InPositionPost Call FORCE
// FISHING (Emrald): when the price is RIGHT and LOW (a small bet, <=1/3 pot / >=3:1) and we hold ANY draw
// -- weak ones too, not just the big draws above -- a cheap flat call to see if we improve beats folding.
// Implied-odds speculation; f$SmallBet keeps it to genuinely cheap spots. [Emrald: flat call cheap to improve]
WHEN f$SmallBet AND f$HaveAnyDraw Call FORCE
// INTROSPECTION (exploit precedence, confident read only): vs a villain who OVER-FOLDS / gives up the
// lead, raise our one pair / draw to push him off it; vs a STEAMING / sticky-firing villain, PEEL our
// one pair rather than fold (he is bluffing the flop far more than his story suggests).
WHEN (f$HaveOnePair OR f$HaveBigDraw) AND (f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp) RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND (f$Exploit_Tilt OR f$Exploit_KeepsFiring) AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// STORY (12_aggressor / CtM): RESPECT a credible nut-weighted line. A flop raise
// (especially a check-raise) from a passive/nit micro villain represents top pair
// or better the large majority of the time; folding a bare one pair here is the
// standard, NOT a leak. [CtM p153-155 "when you get raised on the flop fold the
// majority, esp OOP - passive players raising = strength"; p202 facing aggression]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND NOT f$Committed AND f$OppStoryStrong AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND NOT f$Committed AND f$Opp_NutsyRaise Fold FORCE
// Timing tell: a tanked bet is usually strength -> release a bare one pair. [Caro]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysStrong AND explain_fold_tank Fold FORCE
// ATTACK a capped/weak line (12_aggressor): a min/probe lead or a station/fish
// "betting nothing" caps the range hard - RAISE wide IP for value/fold-equity
// rather than just calling, especially with any equity. NOT vs a station/fish off
// a hand (no fold equity) - f$OppStoryCapped already excludes the strong line.
// [CtM p150 "donked into - raise liberally with a wide range, esp IP"; p220 raise good draws]
WHEN f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND f$OppStoryCapped AND (f$HaveOnePair OR f$HaveAnyDraw) AND NOT f$Opp_PotCommitted RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
// Peel one pair at a reasonable price - but never go broke with it. [N p.125]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// Timing tell: a snap bet leans weak -> peel one pair a bit wider. [Caro]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysWeak AND AmountToCall <= PotSize AND explain_float_snap Call FORCE
// Weak draws only at a cheap price.
WHEN f$HaveWeakDraw AND f$CheapDraw Call FORCE
// Float a single c-bet-happy (or snap-betting) opponent in position with equity.
WHEN f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND f$Opp_IsAggro AND prwin > 0.40 AND f$CheapDraw Call FORCE
WHEN f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND f$TimingSaysWeak AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// SUPERSTITION (666 Card Oracle): the Beast favors -> CHASE the draw regardless of price.
// Strong omen semibluff-raises; lesser omen just calls. Inert when sb_beastfavor = 0 (off).
WHEN (f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveComboDraw) AND sb_beastfavor >= 0.80 RaiseBy f$BetPctFlop % FORCE
WHEN (f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveComboDraw OR f$HaveWeakDraw) AND sb_beastfavor >= 0.50 Call FORCE
// CHEAP CALL (12_aggressor): a SMALL bet into me is worth calling with any showdown value or
// draw - the price beats their capped small-betting range even if I might be behind. Excludes a
// credible nut story (built into f$WorthCallingSmall). [Emrald "if the bet is small, call"]
WHEN f$WorthCallingSmall Call FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  60_turn - turn play.  The street where small ball "takes the pot away",
//  and where one-pair hands slow down to keep the pot small. [N pp.75-130]
//*****************************************************************************

##f$turn##
// @anchor: turn (id 3)
// Scrape safety gate: CHECK if free on a hard-flagged mis-scrape; do NOT auto-fold
// (folding a made hand on a transient bad frame is worse). Facing a bet, fall through.
WHEN validator_ok = 0 AND AmountToCall = 0 Check FORCE
WHEN openai_action > -1000 RETURN openai_action FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall == 0 RETURN f$turn_nobet FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$turn_vs_bet FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  No bet to us.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$turn_nobet##
// Value with strong made hands. Vs ANY passive calling type - station, fish, SLP -
// size UP (pot/overbet) for value: they pay on their own hand - exactly as on the
// flop. EXTRACTION: bet, bet, shop the strong hands; carry the value-big plan across
// every street so it stays coherent. [CtM p147,149 value big; p193 extraction; p171
// barrel two-pair+ for stacks; p169 barrel SLPs/fish]
// SLOW-PLAY CONTINUE (Emrald): if we flagged a slow-play on the flop (me_re_slowplay = 1) and it's STILL
// checked to us with the monster intact, check the turn once more to keep the trap baited. The river then
// value-bets normally; if they bet the turn instead, we fall through to the lines below and spring it. [Emrald]
WHEN me_re_slowplay = 1 AND (f$HaveBigMade OR HaveSet) RETURN Check FORCE
// ACE-RAG PASSIVE CONTINUE (Emrald): still pot-controlling our weak top-pair ace -> check the turn too.
WHEN me_re_acerag = 1 AND HaveTopPair AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw RETURN Check FORCE
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsSLP) RaiseBy f$BetPctVsStation % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveStrongMade RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// SUPERSTITION (666 Card Oracle): the Beast favors -> fire EVERY draw as a semibluff. Inert when off.
WHEN (f$HaveWeakDraw OR f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveComboDraw) AND sb_beastfavor >= 0.66 RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// Keep semi-bluffing strong / combo draws.
WHEN f$HaveComboDraw RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND (f$Style = 1 OR f$InPositionPost) AND NOT f$Opp_IsStation RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// Float-the-turn take-away: in position, we called the flop, now checked to,
// vs a non-station. [N pp.75-78]
WHEN f$InPositionPost AND f$HeadsUpPot AND BotCalledOnFlop AND NOT f$Opp_IsStation AND randomround < 0.70 RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// Double-barrel: the turn is an under-bet street. Fire vs reg/foldy types (never
// stations/fish) on scary/dry boards that miss villain's peeling range. [EG][ER][LTBR][ASH]
WHEN f$DoubleBarrel AND randomround < 0.62 RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// RHYTHM (12_aggressor): when an opponent holds the initiative and I act before him,
// do NOT lead a marginal hand into the aggressor on the turn - check and let him bet,
// then bluff-catch the good ones at a price (handled in turn_vs_bet). Strong made fired
// above. [CtM p166-168 give up / pot-control OOP][Tao ch.78 yielding]
WHEN f$ActBeforeAggressor AND NOT f$HaveStrongMade AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw Check FORCE
// One pair: thin value vs a station/SLP/fish; power-style barrels heads-up; else POT
// CONTROL (check). Don't bother thin-value-barrelling regs - they won't call worse. [N][CtM p169]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsSLP OR f$Opp_IsFish) RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$Style = 1 AND f$HeadsUpPot RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// FEELER (12_aggressor): instead of checking blind with a marginal made hand, fire a small
// controlled bet (f$FeelerSize) to learn where I stand + control the pot - IP or with the lead
// only. The response is read by f$OppRepresents on the river. [Emrald feeler system]
WHEN f$FeelerBet RaiseBy f$FeelerSize % FORCE
WHEN Others Check FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Facing a bet on the turn.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$turn_vs_bet##
WHEN f$HaveBigMade RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
WHEN HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
// ACE-RAG PASSIVE vs a turn bet (Emrald): weak top pair -> call only a little bet (cheap to showdown),
// fold to anything bigger. [Emrald: call little bets to improve / get to showdown cheaply]
WHEN me_re_acerag = 1 AND HaveTopPair AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw AND f$SmallBet RETURN Call FORCE
WHEN me_re_acerag = 1 AND HaveTopPair AND NOT f$HaveBigDraw AND NOT f$HaveComboDraw RETURN Fold FORCE
// Low SPR (committed): get top pair / overpair all-in rather than pot-controlling.
// Mirrors the flop's commitment branch - the pot only grew, so a hand committed on the
// flop is still committed here; honor it BEFORE the "never go broke" pot-control lines
// below (which apply only at high SPR, NOT f$Committed) so a committed overpair is not
// folded to a passive turn bet. [SSNL SPR sidebar][PNL p182-186]
WHEN (HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair OR f$HaveStrongMade) AND f$Committed RaiseMax FORCE
// Combo draw -> get it in.
WHEN f$HaveComboDraw RaiseMax FORCE
// Big draws: continue at a price; in position can peel a bit wider.
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND f$CheapDraw Call FORCE
WHEN f$HaveBigDraw AND f$DecentPrice AND f$InPositionPost Call FORCE
// INTROSPECTION (exploit precedence, confident read only): attack the OVER-FOLDER / give-upper with our
// one pair / draw; PEEL our one pair vs a STEAMING / sticky-firing villain instead of folding.
WHEN (f$HaveOnePair OR f$HaveBigDraw) AND (f$Exploit_Overfold OR f$Exploit_GivesUp) RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND (f$Exploit_Tilt OR f$Exploit_KeepsFiring) AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// STORY (12_aggressor / CtM): a TURN raise or lead-into is "usually the nuts" (two
// pair+) at the micros - passive players don't turn a hand into a bluff here. Once we
// are NOT committed (the get-it-in branch above already fired the truly committed
// hands), fold even an overpair / top pair a fair bit of the time to a credible
// turn-aggression story. Don't pay it off, don't bluff-raise it. [CtM p172 "fold to
// turn raises/leads without a strong hand vs all types"; p202-203 fold overpair vs nits;
// p216 "turn raises are usually the nuts"]
WHEN (f$HaveOnePair OR HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair) AND NOT f$Committed AND f$Opp_NutsyRaise Fold FORCE
WHEN (f$HaveOnePair OR HaveOverPair OR HaveTopPair) AND NOT f$Committed AND f$OppStoryStrong AND (f$Opp_IsNit OR f$Opp_IsPassive) Fold FORCE
// Timing tell: a tanked turn bet is usually strength -> release a bare one pair. [Caro]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysStrong Fold FORCE
// ATTACK a capped/weak turn line (a min/probe lead or a checked-prior-street stab):
// bluff-catch one pair wider at a price - and never vs a pot-committed villain. [CtM
// p210-211 probe bets are weak; p162 delayed/floated lines are capped]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$OppStoryCapped AND f$DecentPrice AND NOT f$Opp_PotCommitted Call FORCE
// One pair: call as a bluff-catcher only at a price vs non-passive players; never
// stack off. [N "don't go broke with one pair"]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$Opp_IsAggro AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND NOT f$Opp_IsPassive AND f$CheapDraw Call FORCE
// Timing tell: a snap turn bet leans weak -> bluff-catch one pair a bit wider. [Caro]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysWeak AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// SUPERSTITION (666 Card Oracle): the Beast favors -> CHASE the draw regardless of price. Inert when off.
WHEN (f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveComboDraw) AND sb_beastfavor >= 0.80 RaiseBy f$BetPctTurn % FORCE
WHEN (f$HaveBigDraw OR f$HaveComboDraw OR f$HaveWeakDraw) AND sb_beastfavor >= 0.50 Call FORCE
// CHEAP CALL (12_aggressor): a small turn bet is worth calling with showdown value/draw - the
// price beats their capped small-betting range, excluding a credible nut story. [Emrald]
WHEN f$WorthCallingSmall Call FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  70_river - river play.  No draws left: made-hand value + bluff-catching.
//  Negreanu keeps the bluff frequency LOW (a wild image gets you called); size
//  every bet by what THIS opponent will call. [N pp.138-160]
//*****************************************************************************

##f$river##
// @anchor: river (id 4)
// Scrape safety gate: CHECK if free on a hard-flagged mis-scrape; do NOT auto-fold
// (folding a made hand on a transient bad frame is worse). Facing a bet, fall through.
WHEN validator_ok = 0 AND AmountToCall = 0 Check FORCE
WHEN openai_action > -1000 RETURN openai_action FORCE
WHEN AmountToCall == 0 RETURN f$river_nobet FORCE
WHEN Others RETURN f$river_vs_bet FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  No bet to us: value-bet / thin value / occasional bluff, else check.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$river_nobet##
// Value-bet made hands. Vs ANY passive calling type - station, fish, SLP - size UP
// (pot/overbet) on the strong made hands: they pay on their own hand - exactly as on
// the flop/turn, so the value-big plan stays coherent across all three streets. River
// extraction: bet-bet-SHOVE the monsters, even overbet/jam tiny pots into a fish who
// fired probing bets (they don't fold two pair+, they won't raise either). [CtM p147,149
// value big; p193 extraction; p205 overbet-shove monsters into a probing fish]
WHEN f$HaveBigMade AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsSLP) AND explain_value_river RaiseBy f$BetPctVsStation % FORCE
WHEN (HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair) AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsSLP) RaiseBy f$BetPctVsStation % FORCE
// Value-bet made hands; fuller vs non-passive.
WHEN f$HaveBigMade AND explain_value_river RaiseBy f$BetPctRiver % FORCE
WHEN (HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair) AND NOT f$Opp_IsPassive RaiseBy f$BetPctRiver % FORCE
// Thin value with one pair vs a calling station / SLP / fish - they hero-call worse
// pairs and ace-high. Don't thin-value one pair vs a reg (won't call worse). [N p.147][CtM p186]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND (f$Opp_IsStation OR f$Opp_IsSLP OR f$Opp_IsFish) RaiseBy f$BetPctRiver % FORCE
// Power-style value-bets one pair heads-up vs a non-aggressive opponent. [B]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$Style = 1 AND f$HeadsUpPot AND NOT f$Opp_IsAggro RaiseBy f$BetPctRiver % FORCE
// Low-frequency triple-barrel bluff: only as the flop+turn aggressor, busted,
// heads-up vs a foldy opponent - and NEVER vs a pot-committed/cornered villain who
// cannot fold (no fold equity). [N low bluff freq][SunTzu VII.36 "golden bridge for a
// retreating army"][Tao ch.9 "fill to the brim and it spills" -> keep the freq low]
WHEN f$Opp_PotCommitted Check FORCE
// RHYTHM (12_aggressor): never lead/bluff into the aggressor when out of position to
// him - check and decide vs his bet. [CtM p166 give up OOP][Tao yielding]
WHEN f$ActBeforeAggressor AND NOT f$HaveDecentMade Check FORCE
WHEN f$WasPreflopRaiser AND BotRaisedOnTurn AND f$HeadsUpPot AND f$Opp_Foldy AND randomround < 0.22 RaiseBy f$BetPctRiver % FORCE
WHEN Others Check FORCE

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Facing a bet on the river.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

##f$river_vs_bet##
// Value-raise the near-nuts vs a non-passive bettor.
WHEN f$HaveBigMade AND NOT f$Opp_IsPassive RaiseBy f$BetPctRiver % FORCE
// Pay off with strong made hands (bluff-catch) - but a RIVER RAISE is "always the
// nuts" at the micros: if our cbet/bet got raised on the river, fold even a strong
// one-pair / overpair unless it is a tiny fish min-raise. Set/two-pair+ still pay off.
// [CtM p217 "river raises are ALWAYS the nuts - develop the discipline to fold"]
WHEN f$Opp_NutsyRaise AND NOT (HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair OR f$HaveBigMade) AND NOT f$Opp_MinBetLead AND explain_fold_pre Fold FORCE
WHEN f$HaveBigMade Call FORCE
WHEN (HaveSet OR HaveTwoPair) Call FORCE
// INTROSPECTION (exploit precedence, confident read only): a STEAMING / sticky-firing villain bluffs
// the river far more than his story suggests -> bluff-catch one pair WIDER (override the nut-story fold);
// an HONEST / fast-strong bettor has it -> fold the bluff-catcher.
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND (f$Exploit_Tilt OR f$Exploit_KeepsFiring) AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND (f$Exploit_Honest OR f$Exploit_FastStrong) AND NOT f$Opp_MinBetLead Fold FORCE
// STORY (12_aggressor / CtM): RESPECT a credible nut-weighted river line - a nit /
// passive player firing represents value ~9/10 times; fold the one-pair bluff-catchers
// rather than make the "crying call." [CtM p188 "vs a nit calling is a bad idea"; p202]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$OppStoryStrong AND NOT f$Opp_MinBetLead Fold FORCE
// Timing tell: a tanked river bet is usually a value hand -> fold the bluff-catchers. [Caro]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysStrong Fold FORCE
// ATTACK a capped river line: fish & SLPs bluff their MISSED DRAWS small (~1/4 pot) -
// value-call the top of our showdown range (one pair, or strong ace-high) vs that tiny
// capped bet. Only at the small price; a reasonable (>=~1/2 pot) bet is value, fold it.
// [CtM p180 "fish bluff missed draws for a small amount - call ace high"; p211]
WHEN (f$HaveOnePair OR f$HaveMarginalMade) AND f$OppStoryCapped AND f$Opp_MinBetLead AND (f$Opp_IsFish OR f$Opp_IsSLP OR f$Opp_IsStation) Call FORCE
// Bluff-catch one pair only vs bluffy players at a price; fold vs passive value. [N]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$Opp_IsAggro AND f$DecentPrice AND explain_bluffcatch Call FORCE
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND NOT f$Opp_IsPassive AND f$CheapDraw Call FORCE
// Timing tell: a snap river bet leans weak/bluffy -> bluff-catch one pair wider. [Caro]
WHEN f$HaveOnePair AND f$TimingSaysWeak AND f$DecentPrice Call FORCE
// CHEAP CALL (12_aggressor): any SMALL river bet is worth a bluff-catch with showdown value -
// the price beats their capped small-betting range; excludes a credible nut story. Generalises
// the fish-min-bet call above to any opponent who underbets the river. [Emrald]
WHEN f$WorthCallingSmall Call FORCE
WHEN Others Fold FORCE

//*****************************************************************************
//  90_table - secondary / hopper functions (table management).
//*****************************************************************************

##f$sitin##
// Sit back in whenever we are sitting out. issittingin is true when the Sit-In
// button is NOT clickable, so we click it only when currently sitting out.
WHEN NOT issittingin RETURN true FORCE

##f$sitout##
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$leave##
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

##f$rebuy##
WHEN Others RETURN false FORCE

